window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"title":"Senior Affiliate Manager — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"affiliate-manager.html","text":"Department Growth (Affiliate Marketing) Hiring Manager Hugo (Head of Affiliation/Partnerships) Location Europe Openings 1 Seniorities Senior Budget $70K–$80K USD base 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role. ⛔️ Top Requirements Manages an active affiliate portfolio with real traffic/conversions. Personally recruited and activated affiliates. Personally negotiates commercial terms and understands the economics. Can identify poor-quality/fraudulent traffic and take action. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For The Function: Affiliate sits under Hugo, our Head of Affiliate/Partnerships, driving growth through third-party traffic — affiliates, media buyers, site owners, socials accounts, etc. — rather than owned channels. The Pace: Fast-moving, performance-driven environment. Landscape shifts overnight (traffic sources, compliance, fraud patterns); the team needs to reprioritize fast without losing execution quality. The Bar: Full-funnel ownership — from recruiting and onboarding affiliates through performance analysis, optimization, and troubleshooting. Not a purely relationship or purely analytical role; both are required daily. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Manages an active affiliate portfolio with real traffic/conversions. Has personally recruited and activated affiliates, not only inherited them. Personally negotiates commercial terms and understands the economics. Can identify poor-quality/fraudulent traffic and take action. Also confirms hands-on experience with affiliate tracking/network platforms (Everflow or equivalent) plus reporting stacks like Looker Studio and SEMrush, and experience across diverse acquisition channels (SEO, media buying, paid social) even if not hands-on executing all of them. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Talks about registered partners rather than active ones. Mainly relationship/account management. Cannot explain traffic quality or deal economics. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Purpose: use the first interview to determine whether the candidate has meaningful affiliate management experience, measurable commercial results, motivation, and communication skills required to progress. Include a summary of answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? Did you test the product? How far did you go — did you create a character, chat, try different features, or mainly browse the website? Are you fully comfortable recruiting and managing affiliates who promote explicit or adult content? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role, what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? How many active affiliates did you personally manage, and what results did your portfolio generate? How many affiliates have you personally recruited vs. inherited or simply managed? What share of your portfolio did you personally source, and how? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Screening should build a clear, quantified picture of: active portfolio ownership, how much was personally sourced (vs. inherited), deal economics (CPA / RevShare / hybrid / flat), and how the candidate manages traffic/source quality and fraud. 📁 Ideal source industries Prioritize sourcing from: adult, webcam, dating, iGaming, casino, betting, affiliate networks, grey/restricted verticals, and other performance-partnership environments — closest match on affiliate model, NSFW/high-scrutiny content comfort, aggressive performance culture, and exposure to fraud/compliance work. 📌 No approved target-company whitelist yet. Hugo has not signed off on a final list — source based on the \"ideal source industries\" above (iGaming/casino/betting, adult/webcam, and similar). Confirm with Hugo before treating any specific company list as validated. Target companies are a sourcing aid, not proof of qualification. Example of ideal/good candidate for calibration: this LinkedIn profile . 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Security Engineer Next → Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager"},{"title":"AI Cinematic Video Editor — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ai-cinematic-video-editor.html","text":"Department R&D Hiring Manager Michael Monin Location Worldwide (CET overlap not required); not actively sourcing in the US/Canada, though an exceptional candidate there can still be considered Contract Starting as a full-time freelancer, then converting to full-time B2B Openings 10 Seniorities Mid or Senior Budget Mid: LATAM $28K–$42K · Europe €42K–€60K. Senior: LATAM $42K–$58K · Europe €60K–€73K. US: up to $95K USD for an exceptional candidate. 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW baseline, compensation-expectations screening, cultural-fit guidance). What follows is specific to this role, including two explicit exceptions to that page's defaults: the mandatory AI-generation requirement, and a higher NSFW bar for MPC / Companion Mode work. ⛔️ Top Requirements Active AI video-generation workflow — hard requirement. Strong cinematic/video storytelling ability. Hands-on generation/prompting, not traditional editing alone. Ability to create coherent stories/sequences using AI-generated material. Strong visual judgment and creative execution. Portfolio/work evidence demonstrating the above. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For We are not hiring a traditional video editor, a motion designer who occasionally experiments with AI, or someone who only assembles footage generated by others. We need a hands-on AI-native cinematic creator/editor who uses current AI-generation tools directly and turns generated material into compelling narrative video — contributing across concept/story, generation, prompting, iteration, shot/sequence selection, editing, pacing, narrative coherence, and final creative execution. Embedded in R&D, working on Candy.ai's content pipeline ( MPC / Companion Mode ) — a deeply technical creative role, not a standard editing position, with high autonomy on execution and technical decisions. Full end-to-end production ownership from concept and prompting through editing, compositing, and final delivery. Iteration culture: test, fail, refine, improve, and share learnings with the team. Engagement: starting as a full-time freelancer, then converting to full-time B2B. Level is determined by portfolio strength, years of relevant experience, and depth of AI pipeline expertise, not format specialization — cinematic-only, short-form-only, and hybrid backgrounds are all welcome. ⛔️ Screening Criteria AI-native creation — currently uses AI-generation tools as a meaningful, regular part of their creative workflow. Look for evidence of tools actually used, prompting/generation ownership, frequency of use, what they personally generate, how they iterate, and how they solve consistency/quality problems. Occasional experimentation with AI is not equivalent to an AI-native workflow. Generation ownership — personally generates the source material, rather than mainly editing assets created by someone else. Storytelling — constructs an actual story, not just attractive individual shots: narrative progression, character consistency, pacing, shot selection, continuity, emotional/creative intent. Visual/cinematic judgment — beyond technical polish: composition, shot choice, movement, pacing, consistency, atmosphere, and the ability to select and improve generated material. End-to-end ownership — can identify what they personally did across concept, writing/story, prompting, generation, editing, sound where relevant, and final assembly. Avoid giving full credit where personal contribution is unclear. Portfolio — must include AI-driven video work. Minimum ~4 years in video production, VFX, or digital art. 🎬 Portfolio evidence to establish: is this actually AI-generated work? What did the candidate personally create? Did they generate the source material and write/develop the story themselves? Which tools were used, and how much iteration did it take? Can they explain the workflow? Is the work coherent across multiple shots — storytelling, not isolated visual experiments? Essential: Current AI video generation tools — Kling, Seedance, Happy Horse, Runway, Pika, and emerging equivalents (active professional use); Premiere Pro, After Effects, or equivalent for final assembly and polish. Also confirms NSFW comfort — 100% dealbreaker if absent, with a hardcore NSFW bar (uncensored models, adult narratives) specifically for MPC / Companion Mode candidates. See the shared Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags guide for the general framework. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Traditional editor with little/no meaningful AI-generation experience; no recent AI-driven portfolio work. AI use is occasional experimentation rather than a real, regular workflow. Edits AI-generated footage but does not personally generate it. Cannot explain their prompts, workflow, or tools. Reel is cinematic-only with no narrative structure, or no demonstrated character/style consistency across sequences. Cannot distinguish personal contribution from collaborators' work. Needs another specialist (colourist, compositor) to deliver a finished sequence, or needs heavy direction rather than working independently from concept to delivery. Visually polished work but weak narrative judgment, or relies heavily on templates/presets without demonstrating creative ownership. Low openness to feedback is a signal to explore during screening, not an automatic reject — see the shared Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags page for company-wide cultural-fit guidance. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What are you doing currently, and why are you considering a move? Walk me through your current workflow — what does a typical production look like from brief to delivery? Which AI video generation tools are you actively using right now, and what are you using them for? Do you personally prompt and generate the material yourself, or mainly edit footage generated by someone else? Share a piece of AI-generated long-form content you're proud of — what were the technical and creative challenges? What did you personally create — concept, story, prompting, generation, editing? Which tools did you use, and how much iteration did it take? How do you maintain character and scene consistency across a longer AI-generated narrative sequence? Have you tried Candy.ai? Our product operates in the adult AI companionship space — are you fully comfortable working with explicit NSFW content on a daily basis? Do you have previous experience working in the adult space? Do you use ComfyUI? If yes, walk me through a workflow you've built. (Bonus signal — not a filter.) If you were able to create anything you wanted without budget constraints or rules, but simply for your pleasure, what would it be? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / engagement (freelancer-to-B2B)? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: Repeated character/scene consistency; narrative mini-series / episodic storytelling. Strong prompting/generation depth; daily use of modern AI creative tools. Strong independent story development; cinematic visual language. Fast experimentation/iteration; ability to combine multiple AI tools effectively. Evidence of shipping significant creative volume without losing quality. Traditional film/video experience can be useful, but it does not substitute for the AI-generation requirement above. Strong plus: ComfyUI — node-based workflow building, customisation, and optimisation; Stable Diffusion / AUTOMATIC1111 (advanced prompting, LoRAs, refining, upscaling, inpainting). Great to have: 3D or VFX background, colourist experience, model training (LoRAs, embeddings, fine-tuning), Photoshop & Design skills. 📁 Sourcing Guidance Ideal backgrounds: AI-native video studios, generative content agencies, or AI filmmaking projects; VFX houses or post-production studios that have moved into generative AI workflows; independent creators with a strong AI video / Stable Diffusion track record; adult content production companies with AI-integrated pipelines (strong bonus). ⚠️ No approved target-company list yet. Source based on the profile above. For adult content production companies, screen carefully against the Off-Limits Companies list before naming any. Confirm with Michael before treating any specific company list as validated. Target companies are a sourcing aid only — a candidate from an unlisted company is assessed on the same bar. 🔄 Interview Process Role-specific exception to the shared default (see ⏳ Hiring Process ): no dedicated Hiring Manager stage and no references. A portfolio review can happen as pre-screening, ahead of the recruiter call — it is not a formal interview stage. The case study is a paid assignment; duration is set per candidate. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Paid Case Study → 3 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 4 Offer ← Previous Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer Next → Senior Product Designer"},{"title":"AI Legal Specialist — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ai-legal-specialist.html","text":"🗄️ Not currently open. Kept for reference — do not submit against this role. Department Operations Team Legal Hiring Manager Maxwelle Sokol (Legal & Safety Lead) Location Europe (CET overlap required, 4+ hrs/day) Contract B2B preferred Openings 1 Seniorities Junior, Mid Priority Closed Budget Up to €85K (total package) 🧑‍🧑‍🧒‍🧒 Team & Environment Context The Product: Candy.ai — an AI companionship platform. Candidates will be exposed to uncensored, NSFW AI-generated content as part of the job (testing/reviewing the platform) — must be 100% comfortable with that. The Role: A generalist Compliance seat owning legal/compliance workflows across data protection (GDPR — DPAs, TIAs), AI governance documentation, product/feature compliance reviews, IP (DMCA, copycats), contract review (NDAs, licenses), and legal terms upkeep (ToS, Privacy Notice, content policy). Guided by and works side-by-side with Maxwelle Sokol (Legal & Safety Lead, US-trained lawyer, 10+ years litigation/in-house). The Focus: Breadth over depth — the JD explicitly doesn't expect experience in every category, but does expect a doer mindset and motivation to learn unfamiliar legal areas fast. The Bar: A generalist who can handle the wide array of legal/compliance topics that come in. We don't expect experience in every category listed — a doer mindset and motivation to learn is non-negotiable. 🎯 Calibration Anchors & Target Profiles ⛔️ Non-Negotiables Legal education — Masters of Law, JD, or recognized legal certification. Not necessarily a licensed attorney. 2–6 years relevant experience , including at least 2 years working with contracts generally and data protection law specifically (e.g. GDPR, CCPA, LGPD) — can speak concretely to preparing a DPA/TIA and has experience contacting vendors on contract issues. NSFW comfort — 100% dealbreaker; must be comfortable reviewing and discussing uncensored AI-generated content directly. Fluent, plain-English communicator — can distill complex legal concepts for non-legal stakeholders. Doer mindset / generalist adaptability — balances execution, planning, and strategy; comfortable picking up unfamiliar compliance topics without a narrow specialist lane. Backbone with stakeholders — can push back and say no on compliance grounds, even under pressure to move fast, without being obstructive for its own sake. ✨ Nice-to-have Full attorney/legal counsel certification Experience in high-growth startups, B2C, and/or AI compliance specifically Additional language fluency 📋 Evaluation Framework 1. Legal & Compliance Execution — 40% Legal education plus 2–6 years as legal counsel or similar, including at least 2 years on contracts and data protection law specifically — can speak concretely to preparing a DPA/TIA, contacting vendors on contract issues, and the day-to-day compliance workload (IP, contract reviews, terms updates, tracking legal developments). Hard Filters: no legal education; no contracts or data-protection experience. 2. Doer Mindset, Ownership & Humility — 25% Goal-oriented, takes ownership and commitment; balances execution, planning, and strategy; humble and open to feedback, willing to learn unfamiliar legal topics rather than staying in a narrow lane. Hard Filters: not coachable; no delivery language; unwilling to work outside a narrow specialty. 3. Communication & Cross-functional Collaboration — 20% Distills complex legal concepts into plain English for non-legal stakeholders; strong, collaborative communicator; fully fluent in English; works well with regular guidance from Maxwelle Sokol. Has the backbone to push back and say no to stakeholders on compliance grounds, even under pressure to move fast. Hard Filters: can't explain legal concepts in plain English; not fluent in English; can't meet the 4+ hr/day CET overlap; folds under stakeholder pressure instead of holding a compliance line. 4. NSFW Comfort & AI Interest — 15% Genuinely comfortable reviewing and discussing uncensored, NSFW AI-generated content; professional experience with or interest in AI. Hard Filters: hesitant or moralizes on the NSFW question. 💬 Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. Our product involves AI companionship and uncensored, adult-oriented content — you'd be reviewing and discussing NSFW material directly as part of this role. Are you fully comfortable with that? Walk me through your experience with data protection law — have you prepared a DPA or Transfer Impact Assessment? What did that process actually involve? Do you have experience in trust & safety or moderation on online platforms? Tell me about it. This role spans GDPR, AI governance documentation, IP, contract review, and policy updates — a generalist mix. How do you approach picking up an unfamiliar legal area quickly? Do you have professional experience in the online B2C context? Tell me about it. Tell me about a time you had to push back on a stakeholder or say no on compliance grounds — even when there was pressure to move fast. What happened, and how did you handle it? What are the top 2–3 things you're looking for in your next opportunity? ← Previous AI Marketing Video Editor"},{"title":"AI LLM Tech Lead — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ai-llm-tech-lead.html","text":"🗄️ Not currently open. Kept for reference — do not submit against this role. Department R&D Hiring Manager Michael Monin (CTO & Co-founder) Location Worldwide Budget $200K + $150K equity OR $250K + $80K equity Contract B2B preferred Openings 1 Seniorities Lead Priority Closed 🧑‍🧑‍🧒‍🧒 Team & Environment Context This is not a research role and not a pure people-management role. We want a builder who has done the hard technical work themselves — and can also lead a small team of AI engineers from the front. The mission: own the \"brain\" and architecture of our core product at EverAI / Candy.ai — the conversational AI experience that is central to everything we do. The Lead will not have time to learn hard skills on the job. They need to arrive with hands-on fine-tuning experience already behind them. The Content: Primarily Candy.ai. Candidates must be 100% comfortable working with NSFW/explicit training data and building moderation for it. NSFW background is a plus, not a requirement. Remote, fast-paced scale-up environment. No bureaucracy, no long feedback loops. ⚠️ Critical Context: The most important thing is not the scale of tokens or infrastructure — it's whether the AI/chatbot product they worked on was core to the business . A candidate who built a central, user-facing conversational product at a company of 500K+ users is more relevant than someone who optimized inference at a large company where AI was a side feature. 🎯 Calibration Anchors & Target Profiles We are looking for candidates where the conversational AI or chatbot was the product — not a feature. Consumer AI & Companion Platforms Creative & Roleplay AI High-Scale Conversational Products LLM-first startups where the chat experience is the core value proposition Minimum size guidance: the AI should have been the central revenue-generating and/or impactful feature of the business (it does not matter if it's B2B or B2C). ⛔️ Non-Negotiables Hands-on fine-tuning experience — must have done it themselves, for external user-facing products (not internal tooling). Key question: what did you fine-tune, and why? Fine-tuning must represent ~60%+ of their AI experience (agentic AI / RAG / prompt engineering alone is not a fit). Post-training experience is mandatory; pre-training is a nice-to-have. The AI product was core / critical to the business — not a side project, not an internal tool. It's about ownership, impact and risk. Scope includes LLMs and Computer Vision — both are valid. Leadership experience is a must — being senior is not enough. Minimum 1–2 years of hands-on leadership experience required. Must still be technically hands-on. Strong English communication skills — this role requires clear technical and cross-functional communication. NSFW comfort — must be comfortable with explicit training data and content moderation in this context. ℹ️ Good Keywords to Look out for Models & frameworks — core: Mistral · Llama · DeepSeek · Qwen · Hugging Face Production & inference — strong signal: vLLM · PyTorch · inference optimization · open-source LLM Fine-tuning techniques — high signal: SFT · RLHF · DPO · LoRA · QLoRA · PEFT Fine-tuning frameworks — niche, very high signal: Axolotl · Unsloth · LitGPT 📋 Evaluation Framework 1. Fine-Tuning & Model Alignment — 40% Has personally fine-tuned models for external, user-facing products. Understands SFT, RLHF, and DPO not just in theory but from direct experience. Can speak concretely to what they fine-tuned, why, and what the outcome was. Familiar with data engineering — curating, cleaning, and synthetic data generation. Hard Filters: Fine-tuning experience limited to internal tooling or demos; cannot describe a specific fine-tuning project and its business impact; prompt engineering only. 2. Technical Leadership — 25% Player/coach profile. Sets technical direction and owns the architecture while remaining hands-on in the codebase. Has led small teams of senior engineers, conducted code reviews, and maintained a technical roadmap. Does not delegate everything — writes code. Hard Filters: Pure managers who no longer code; pure ICs with no leadership experience. 3. Production Engineering — 25% Has shipped conversational AI to real users at scale. Comfortable with the modern LLM stack: PyTorch, Hugging Face, vLLM or equivalent inference engines. Understands latency, throughput, and cost trade-offs in production — not just in benchmarks. Hard Filters: Academic or research-only profiles; no production deployment experience. 4. Content Moderation Architecture — 10% Understands how to build nuanced, context-aware moderation — not binary safe/unsafe filters. Knows the difference between lazy safety filtering and intelligent classifier-based moderation. NSFW experience is a plus, not a hard requirement. Hard Filters: Strong ideological objection to working with NSFW content or explicit training data. 💬 Pre-Screen Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What is your current situation, and why are you considering leaving? Why did you leave your last 2 workplaces? Are you comfortable working on a product that involves NSFW content — including working with explicit training data and building moderation for it? Tell me about a model you fine-tuned for a live, user-facing product. What was the goal, what did you actually do, and what was the outcome? Was the AI/chatbot product you worked on the core of the business, or a feature within a larger product? What is your philosophy on model alignment (SFT vs. RLHF/DPO) for a creative, roleplay-centric product? How do you balance safety with steerability? Which open-source models (e.g. Llama 3, Mistral) have you been working with recently? What are their strengths and limitations for conversational use cases? ⁉️ FAQs Technical 1. Model Strategy & Ownership Are you building proprietary models, or fine-tuning open-source / API models? We fine-tune open-source models and also use some APIs. The majority of our traffic — roughly 80–90% — runs on self-hosted fine-tuned open-source models. What % of usage is OpenAI / Anthropic APIs vs self-hosted? 10–20% third-party API, 80–90% self-hosted fine-tuned models. What is your long-term model strategy? Our strategy is to stay on top of the frontier of open-source models and fine-tune them to match our user preferences. We've tested very large open-source models, and our smaller in-house fine-tuned model still outperforms them on our roleplay evaluation metrics. Roleplay is a highly specific use case, and we believe owning the fine-tuning loop is a durable edge. How differentiated is your model vs competitors? On our internal roleplay evals, our fine-tuned smaller model outperforms significantly larger out-of-the-box open-source and closed-source models. We haven't run a formal head-to-head benchmark against competitor products, but our qualitative signal — user retention, session length, and like rates — suggests a meaningful quality gap in our favor for this specific use case. 2. Infrastructure & Scale What is the infra stack (cloud, orchestration, serving)? Everything runs on GKE, managed by a 5-person DevOps team. How are you handling your token volume technically? We serve multi-billion tokens/day of combined input/output on GKE, running across a mix of GPU types. Latency benchmarks? Kept private. We target sub-2 second P50 latency on self-hosted models for the chat experience. Cost per request? Kept private, but cost-efficiency is a core optimization axis given our scale. GPU setup / budget? Budget kept private. Stack runs on modern datacenter GPUs on GKE, e.g. H100s/A100s, RTX PRO. Any bottlenecks today (infra vs model vs product)? On the infra side, the main challenge is serving larger models (32B+) at efficient speed and cost. But the bigger challenge is on the modeling side — training a state-of-the-art roleplay model. That's precisely where this hire comes in. 3. Data & Training Pipelines What is the source of training data? A mix of sources including curated internal data and synthetic generation. Specific breakdowns are kept private, but the candidate would have meaningful data to work with from day one. User conversations? Synthetic generation? Yes, synthetic generation is part of the mix. Details on both kept private. How do you handle data labeling? We have an internal process in place. Specifics kept private, but scaling and improving the labeling pipeline is one of the areas we expect this hire to help evaluate. Preference data for RLHF/DPO? Yes, we run preference-based post-training. The maturity of this pipeline and how to scale it is one of the concrete areas the new hire would help shape. What tooling exists for experiment tracking / evaluation? We have tooling in place for both. Specifics kept private, but improving experimentation velocity and evaluation maturity are part of the scope. How mature is your eval framework (offline + online)? Offline: solid and roleplay-specific. Online: earlier stage — this is explicitly part of the 90-day scope. 4. Moderation & Safety How does EverGuard actually work? It's a hybrid approach combining model-based classifiers and rules. Specific architecture details are kept private. What % of engineering effort is moderation vs core product? Around 25% moderation, 75% core product. What are the hardest unsolved moderation problems today? The hardest ongoing challenges are around context-dependent nuance — staying permissive enough for legitimate creative/roleplay use cases while catching genuinely harmful patterns, and keeping false-positive rates low so the experience doesn't feel over-censored. These are active areas of work rather than blockers. Any regulatory exposure? (EU AI Act risk, etc.) No material exposure at this time. We monitor the regulatory landscape proactively. 5. Architecture & Engineering Reality What does the current system architecture look like end-to-end? Specifics kept private, but the stack is GKE-based with self-hosted inference, a fine-tuning pipeline, moderation layer, and the product surface. Where is the biggest technical debt? Our training pipeline could be more automated and easier to iterate on — today, running a new fine-tuning cycle takes more manual orchestration than we'd like. Our online eval infrastructure is also less mature than our offline side. Both are explicitly part of the scope for this hire. How mature is CI/CD? Monitoring? Incident handling? CI/CD and monitoring are functional but have room to improve — solid foundation on core infra, less mature on model-level observability. Incident handling is strong, with clear on-call rotations and a good uptime track record. How often are models deployed to production? Every 2–3 months depending on cycles and team focus. A faster release cadence is something we want to move toward. 6. Product Performance & Metrics What are the core success metrics for AI quality? Retention, revenue per user, session length, and like rates. What are current failure modes in user experience? The biggest one is personalization — we serve a user base with very different preferences (short messages vs long narrative, different content styles, different roleplay patterns) and our current model doesn't yet adapt dynamically enough to each user. There are also the usual roleplay-model failure modes: occasional consistency drift over long sessions, and edge cases where the model doesn't quite hit the desired tone. Where is the biggest gap — Intelligence / Latency / Safety? Primarily intelligence and personalization. Latency and safety are in a good place today, though we keep investing in both. 7. Immediate Scope for This Hire What are the top 3 problems this person must solve in 90 days? (1) Deeply understand our current training pipeline, identify bottlenecks, and propose concrete improvements. (2) Work closely with the engineering team to upgrade our fine-tuning pipeline, and partner with the CTO and leadership to define the success metrics and KPIs that define what \"a better model\" actually means for us. (3) Bring product-minded ideas for how to push the roleplay chat experience to the next level, in close collaboration with the product team. By the end of 90 days, the expectation is a clear plan for what a better model looks like, plus concrete initiatives to improve the in-chat user experience. What is currently blocking growth that this hire unlocks? Two things. First, it frees up significant CTO bandwidth. Second, and more importantly, it brings dedicated ML leadership into the room. Our CTO's background is in web engineering, and we want a peer who owns the ML depth — someone who can partner with him on technical direction and push our AI engineers on the modeling decisions that will define the next phase of the product. How much freedom vs alignment with CTO? Trust is earned, and ownership is granted as soon as trust is established. We value people who take real ownership and move fast. Non-Technical / Commercial 1. Business Model & Monetisation How do you make money today? Subscriptions and token-based monetization. What % of users are active (DAU/MAU) / paying? ARPU / LTV? All specific numbers kept private at this stage. Happy to share more context with candidates who reach the later interview stages under NDA. 2. Growth Quality \"50M users\" → how many are real vs bots? We have captcha plus email confirmation, so bot contamination is low. The vast majority are real users. Retained after 30 days? Kept private. Happy to discuss ranges with candidates in later stages. What channels drove growth? (viral vs paid) Kept private at this stage. 3. Competitive Landscape Who do you see as direct competitors? Character.ai and Replika in the mainstream roleplay space. In the NSFW-oriented segment, Ourdream.ai and Lovescape. We view ourselves as differentiated on model quality for the roleplay use case specifically. 4. Team & Hiring Plan What is the target team size in 6–12 months? Depends on needs and the business trajectory — we hire based on clear impact, not headcount targets. Will this hire become Head of AI, or stay as senior IC / player-coach? We're still a small company, so everything is possible. Anyone who shows extreme dedication, motivation, and business impact can grow into larger responsibilities. The initial framing is senior IC / player-coach with a clear path upward. What other hires are planned around them? None currently planned for the next 3–6 months, unless a specific project with high business impact justifies it. 5. Culture Reality Check What does \"high performance\" actually mean here? Ownership, curiosity, strong motivation, good attitude, and measurable business impact. Hours / output expectations? We optimize for output and impact, not hours. That said, we move fast and expect people to match that energy. Any recent attrition? No material attrition issues. How are disagreements handled? A quick 1:1 or a focused call with the relevant stakeholders to align on direction. We value speed of decision-making. 6. Risk & Controversy Past platform bans? Payment provider issues? PR issues due to NSFW positioning? None on all three. How do you mitigate platform risk (Apple/Google policies)? No issues today. Our positioning and compliance posture keep us clear of platform problems. 7. Compensation Clarity Equity = $80k total or annual? Total. Package is competitive and structured for the long term. Flexibility on base? The package is competitive and we can structure it for the right profile. Specifics to be discussed with your TA contact. Any upside tied to growth milestones? Not part of the current structure. Next → AI Marketing Video Editor"},{"title":"AI Marketing Video Editor — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ai-marketing-video-editor.html","text":"🗄️ Not currently open. Kept for reference — do not submit against this role. Department Growth Hiring Manager Thomas Lacroix (CMO & Co-founder) Location Worldwide (CET overlap not required) Contract B2B preferred Openings 2 Seniorities Mid or Senior Priority Closed Budget Mid: LATAM $28K–$42K · Europe €42K–€65K · US/Canada $60K–$80K. Senior: LATAM $42K–$58K · Europe €65K–€80K · US/Canada $80K–$100K. 📌 We are looking for Video Editors who specialize in paid social ads — specifically Meta and TikTok. This is not a generalist editing role and not a cinematic/narrative role. Every edit must be built to convert: hook in the first 2 seconds, fast iteration, data-driven decisions. Daily work involves NSFW and explicit creatives for Candy.ai. Do not submit candidates unless NSFW comfort has been explicitly confirmed on a call. 🧑‍🧑‍🧒‍🧒 Team & Environment Context The Team: Reports directly to the CMO, working alongside 3 Creatives. The candidate can be Mid or Senior. High-Velocity Pipeline: We move at the speed of AI. They must manage their own pipeline independently — from idea inception to final color grading and sound design. The Content: Candy.ai. We operate in the AI companionship space. 100% comfort with NSFW/explicit creatives is a non-negotiable baseline requirement. Data-Obsessed Iteration: We iterate based on KPIs (CTR, CR). If an ad doesn't perform, we don't fix it — we pivot and cut a new version immediately. AI-Mandatory Workflow: AI is core to how we work, not a bonus skill. Candidates must be prompt engineers who use Midjourney, Runway, KlingAI, or equivalent tools to create assets that don't yet exist. 🎯 Calibration Anchors & Target Profiles Ideal backgrounds: High-volume DTC agencies, Gaming, iGaming, or Dating/Social app marketing Company examples: Tango Me, Kilo Health, V-Shred, TubeScience, etc. Bonus: prior experience in Adult, Dating, or iGaming industries ⛔️ Non-Negotiables NSFW comfort — 100% dealbreaker; must be explicitly confirmed before submission Paid social portfolio — majority must be Meta and/or TikTok ads; no cinematic-only portfolios Performance mindset — understands Hook-Body-CTA; can cut multiple hook variations for the same ad; knows what a retention graph is and how to act on it Full technical autonomy — handles sound design, colour grading, and motion graphics independently; does not require a separate sound engineer, colorist, or motion designer to finish a 30-second ad AI fluency — uses generative AI tools (Midjourney, Runway, KlingAI, or equivalent) in daily professional workflow; not resistant to AI; sees it as a primary tool Speed — first draft within hours; multiple iterations per week Fluent English — can communicate clearly about creative decisions and performance rationale 🛠️ Tools Essential: Premiere Pro and/or Davinci Resolve and/or Final Cut and/or Avid Media Composer. Very important: After Effects, Photoshop. Great to have: Illustrator, Figma, Eleven Labs, Topaz. Amazing to have: ComfyUI. AI tools/platforms great to have proficiency in: Kling AI, VEO, Sora, Nano Banana, Midjourney, Runway, Qwen, Higgsfield, Heygen. 📋 Evaluation Framework 1. Performance-Driven Storytelling — 35% Deep understanding of the Hook-Body-CTA framework. Can manipulate pacing, motion, and sound to drive user action. Able to look at a retention graph and identify exactly where users drop off. Comfortable cutting multiple hook variations for the same ad to find the winning angle. Can optimise for multiple formats (9:16, 1:1, 16:9) and channel-specific best practices (TikTok style vs. adult pre-roll). Hard Filters: Cinematic-only portfolios. If the first 2 seconds of their work don't grab attention — reject. 2. Generative AI & Tool Mastery — 30% Proven experience using generative AI tools (Midjourney, Stable Diffusion, Runway, Luma, KlingAI, etc.) in a professional workflow. Uses AI for advanced tasks: generating custom B-roll, face-swapping, generative fill, AI-voice integration. Deep expertise in Adobe Premiere Pro, After Effects, or equivalent. Hard Filters: Resistance to AI tools or a traditional-only mindset. If they see AI as a threat rather than a primary tool, they won't fit. 3. Technical Autonomy & Sound Design — 20% Fully independent in the editing process — including sound design, color grading, and motion graphics in After Effects. Manages their own render queues, file structures, and technical exports for high-volume, daily iteration. Hard Filters: Requires a separate sound engineer, colorist, or motion designer to finish a 30-second ad. 4. Startup Grit & Communication — 15% Perfectly fluent English. Can explain why an edit will convert a specific target audience. Thrives in fast, messy environments. Willing to kill an edit they spent hours on and start over if the data says to. Prioritizes speed and performance over artistic prestige. Hard Filters: High sensitivity to NSFW content; needs more than 48 hours for a first draft; job-hoppers under 1 year; no concrete recent win stories. 💬 Pre-Screen Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. Walk me through your current role — what type of content do you produce day to day? Is it primarily for paid marketing, organic, or something else? What does your AI workflow look like? Which tools do you use, and for what specific tasks? Have you worked on performance marketing creatives — paid social, pre-roll, or direct response ads? What platforms? Walk me through a recent ad you're proud of — what was the brief, what did you create, and how did it perform? Have you tried Candy.ai? Our product operates in the adult AI companionship space — are you fully comfortable working with NSFW content on a daily basis? ← Previous AI LLM Tech Lead Next → AI Legal Specialist"},{"title":"Senior Product Manager — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ai-product-manager.html","text":"Department R&D Hiring Manager Pierre Gerbaud (Product Lead) Location Europe Openings 2 Seniorities Senior Budget Up to €120K (total package) 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role, including one explicit exception to that page's defaults. ⛔️ Top Requirements AI-native — active, meaningful use of AI in their actual product-building workflow (hard requirement, not a positive signal). Hands-on builder — prototypes, experiments and validates ideas rather than operating only through specs/coordination. Strong B2C product experience. Strong product judgment — moves from user/problem → experiment → shipped result. Comfortable operating with high autonomy and fast iteration. Demonstrates personal ownership and measurable product outcomes. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For A hands-on, technical PM at the intersection of product, AI, data, and engineering — not a typical PM whose work is primarily roadmaps, tickets, and handing specs to engineering. Reports to Pierre Gerbaud (Product Lead). This person identifies opportunities, prototypes and tests ideas quickly using AI tools directly, and pushes experiments toward production — high agency, moves fast with minimal oversight. ⛔️ Screening Criteria AI-native working style — actively uses modern AI tools (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, or similar) in their actual workflow and can explain concretely how. Builder / prototyping ability — personally prototypes and ships, rather than relying entirely on engineering/design to validate every idea; has shipped a real prototype, experiment, or feature end-to-end. B2C product depth — worked on consumer products where user behaviour, engagement, monetization, retention, or experimentation outcomes matter. Product judgment — can explain what problem they identified, why they prioritized it, what they personally did, what was tested/shipped, what happened, and what they learned or changed. Ownership — demonstrates personal ownership rather than describing only what \"the team\" delivered. Speed / experimentation — comfortable testing, learning and iterating rather than requiring long planning cycles before action. 📎 Professional evidence is strongly preferred; an exceptional side project may still count if it shows production-level complexity, iteration, and ownership — it should not be just a landing page or toy demo. 🔒 AI usage is a hard gate for this role. Company-wide, AI usage is generally a positive signal rather than mandatory (see Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags ) — but Senior Product Manager is one of only four roles where it's an explicit requirement, alongside Product Designer, Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer, and AI Cinematic Video Editor/Creator. Do not submit a candidate who cannot show hands-on, personal AI-building experience for this role. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 PM work is mainly coordination, roadmaps, Jira/ticket management or stakeholder management. Cannot give concrete examples of personally building/prototyping/testing. No meaningful current AI-tool usage. Talks about AI conceptually but does not use it in their own workflow. Cannot separate personal contribution from team output. Vague product impact with no measurable outcome. Primarily enterprise/internal-tool background without convincing transferable B2C product depth. Depends on engineering/design for every prototype or validation step. Cannot explain why an experiment/product decision succeeded or failed. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What are you doing currently, and why are you considering a move now? Why EverAI? Have you tried Candy.ai ? What do you think about it? Our product involves AI companionship and uncensored, adult-oriented content. Are you fully comfortable building and shipping features in this category? Walk me through a specific feature or prototype you personally built and shipped using AI coding tools — how did you use AI to write code, analyze data, or contribute pull requests, and what was your process? What AI tools or techniques have you sought out and tried on your own initiative, beyond what a specific project required? How do you validate what they produce? Tell me about a recent product idea you personally moved from concept toward something testable or shipped. Did you prototype it yourself, what tools did you use, and how quickly did you get to validation? What was the highest impact (on revenue or similar) feature you've worked on? What was the problem, your hypothesis, the decision you made, the metric you tracked, the result, and what you learned? Which of your product experience is genuinely consumer-facing (B2C) rather than enterprise/internal tooling? What are the top 2–3 things you're looking for in your next opportunity? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: B2C entertainment, gaming, consumer subscription, or social/creator products. Highly experimental consumer products. Demonstrated side projects / prototypes shipped with AI tools. Technical fluency and a strong experimentation background. Evidence of building things independently. Design fluency — can prompt a decent UI to stay autonomous (valuable, not a blocker for an otherwise strong candidate). Growth trajectory > experience. Don't over-index on seniority or years of experience — a candidate with real agency, curiosity, and momentum can be a stronger fit than someone more senior without that trajectory. A non-traditional path into PM (e.g. a developer or designer who grew into product) is welcome, not a concern. ❓ Why does a non-traditional path fit this well? Classic PM career progression is built around not coding — writing specs, running standups, delegating to engineers. The people who've spent years doing that are the population least likely to have picked up hands-on AI-coding fluency, precisely because that wasn't their job. The people who do have that fluency right now tend to be recent converts — people who just started operating in a PM-adjacent capacity, not people with a multi-year PM career behind them. 📎 Always ask for a portfolio, GitHub profile, repository, live project, or demo — the single best signal for AI-native building. Do not source from direct AI-companionship/AI-dating competitors (Replika, Character.AI, and similar) — this is not what we're looking for. 📁 Sourcing Guidance Industry Target companies B2C entertainment/consumer — primary (genuinely scale-up stage) Duolingo, Discord, Whatnot, Locket, Suno B2C entertainment/consumer — secondary (mature, but still runs heavy internal experimentation) Netflix, Spotify, Snap, TikTok/ByteDance Gaming — primary (fast A/B-test cultures, scale-up stage) Voodoo, SuperPlay, Homa Games, Kwalee Gaming — secondary (large/acquired studios, still experimentation-heavy) Scopely, Zynga, King, Supercell, Miniclip, Playtika Companies where PM-as-builder is the norm (closest match for the AI-native trait) Linear, Vercel, Notion, Ramp, Retool, Replit, Cursor, Windsurf, Perplexity, early-stage YC-style startups generally ℹ️ Sourcing aid only, not an automatic qualifier or rejection rule — a strong candidate from outside these pools should still be considered. The first four pools cover background fit only, not AI-coding fluency; the PM-as-builder pool (strongest for AI-native fluency) skews B2B/dev-tools, not B2C — the two preferences may not always show up in the same candidate. 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager Next → Content Moderator"},{"title":"How to Use Ashby — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ashby.html","text":"How to Use Ashby (our ATS) 🪜 Using Ashby: A Step-by-Step Guide for Recruitment Agencies 1 Step 1: Access Ashby Receive Your Invite : Upon being granted access, you should receive an automatic invitation from Ashby. An example of the invite email is shown below 👇 Log In : Use the credentials provided in the email to log into Ashby using this link . You should be able to see the log in options, as below 👇 If you encounter any login issues, check with your TA contact to confirm your account setup. Familiarize Yourself : Once logged in, take some time to explore the Ashby interface. Key sections to familiarize yourself with include: Candidate Dashboard : Manage candidates, their statuses, and associated details. Job Requisitions : View job openings assigned to you and their hiring pipelines. Reports and Metrics : Access data-driven insights for recruitment performance. 2 Step 2: Navigating the Home Page - Key Areas and Features Welcome to Your Ashby Home Screen: Once logged in, you'll arrive at your Home Screen , the central hub for accessing Ashby's key features. From here, you can efficiently manage, add, and track candidates throughout the recruitment process. Get to know and Understand the Key things you will need: The screenshot above ☝️ outlines the seven key areas of the Ashby home page, designed to streamline your recruitment workflow: Candidates: Access the Candidate Pipeline to view where candidates are in the hiring process. Use Candidate Search to filter candidates with basic or advanced search options. Jobs : Open the Jobs Dashboard to see a high-level summary of candidates across different stages for each job. Notifications : View and manage your notifications within Ashby from this section. Add : Use the +Add button to manually add a new candidate to a job requisition. Search : Quickly search for candidates or jobs using Command + K (Mac) or CTRL + K (Windows). Personal Settings : Update your profile settings such as avatar, timezone, and notification preferences. Tasks : Access your tasks when you're @mentioned in notes on candidate profiles. You can respond directly from this section. 3 Step 3: Add New Candidates Navigate to Add Candidate : Click the +Add button, located in the top-right corner. Select Add Candidate from the dropdown. Enter Candidate Information : Upload the CV : Use the CV Upload feature to add the candidate's resume. Ashby will automatically parse and fill in most of the candidate's details, such as their name, email, and phone number. Illustration here: Verify or Fill In Missing Information : Double-check the parsed information and manually fill in any missing details: Name : Ensure the candidate's full name is accurate. Email : Confirm the email address provided. Phone Number : Add or verify their contact number. Verify the Attribution (Ownership) of the Candidate: When you add a candidate to Ashby, the platform automatically attributes the source to you and your recruitment agency. Illustration here: Add Social Links to the Candidate's Profile: Click on the + Add button. In the dropdown, select the type of link: LinkedIn (mandatory) : For all candidates (always add it, if the candidate has a LinkedIn profile). Website (optional): you can use the Website option for any additional websites, portfolios, blogs, or relevant URLs. GitHub/StackOverflow/Medium/Twitter (optional) Illustration here: Once you click on Next , add the Candidate to an Open Job: Select the Open Job : On the next screen, you will see a list of available job requisitions. Use the search bar or scroll to find the relevant job title. Assign the Candidate : Click on the job title to select it. Ensure the job matches the candidate's profile and skillset. Double-check the Attribution, if needed, as mentioned before. Illustration here: Click on Add to Job , to finalize. Tutorial video: A video walkthrough of this step exists internally but isn't publicly shareable yet. Ask your TA contact if you'd like to see it. 4 Step 4: Check Candidates' Profiles The Candidate Profile in Ashby is the central hub for managing and viewing all candidate details. It allows you to keep track of their progress and collaborate with your team effectively. Here's a breakdown of the key areas: 1. Activities and Progress: View the candidate's progress through the interview stages. Track where they are in the hiring pipeline and update their status as needed. 2. Summary: Find essential candidate details such as: Name Email Location Quickly access the most important information at a glance. 3. Resume: Access and view the candidate's uploaded resume. Ensure the document is complete and formatted correctly. 4. Feed: View a chronological log of all activities related to the candidate, including: Notes Feedback Emails (if you have the necessary permissions). Use the Notes and Emails filters to customize your view and focus on specific updates. 5. Notes: Here, you can add detailed notes about the candidate, including observations or next steps. Mandatory: Use @mentions to involve other team members and assign tasks. Please assign your TA contact to ALL candidates you add by @mentioning them, ensuring proper visibility. Mandatory: Write down a note with this template: Location/Timezone: Visa/Right to Work: LinkedIn Profile: Portfolio or GitHub: (if applicable only) Salary Expectations: Preferred Currency for Salary payment: Type of Contract: Availability: Notice Period: Other Offers/Recruitment processes: Interview Recording Link: Notes/Summary: Check the Create Task box to turn the note into a task for better tracking and accountability. ⚠️ Tutorial video here: ▶ Watch the Ashby walkthrough on Loom 🛠️ Other Features Candidate Pipeline The Candidate Pipeline allows you to view your candidates across jobs and stages. You can use the search bar to search for specific candidates and the filters to pull candidates that meet specific criteria. From there, you can click on the arrow next to a job to view the pipeline and the candidates in each stage. 1) Search - Search for a candidate by name here. 2) Filters - Filter by specific criteria to pull the candidates you're looking for here. 3) Jobs and pipelines - jobs you have access to will be listed here, click the arrow to the left of the job title to open the pipeline and view the candidates in each stage. Tasks When someone @mentions you on a candidate's profile, or you have an overdue task to submit feedback on a candidate, a task will be created on your home page. You'll receive notifications via email until the task is resolved. Personal Settings Your Personal Settings are where you manage account settings specific to you, including your name, avatar, and notification settings. Under Notifications, you have the option to enable or disable email notifications for when: You are mentioned in a note A candidate is hired A candidate is moved to a new interview stage Someone replies to a note that you wrote You have overdue tasks (report sent daily) 💡 Additional Tips Using the Ashby Chrome Extension Install the Ashby Chrome Extension to add candidates directly from LinkedIn. Visit a candidate's LinkedIn profile, open the extension, and click \"Add to Ashby\" to import their information. Bulk Importing Candidates For adding multiple candidates simultaneously, use Ashby's bulk import feature. Ensure your data file is formatted correctly to match Ashby's requirements. 🆘 For more info and tutorials, please visit Ashby's Knowledge Base . Thank you! Next → Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags"},{"title":"Business Analyst — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"business-analyst.html","text":"Department Operations Team Operations Hiring Manager Simas (Operations Manager) Location Worldwide. Asia or Europe preferred. Openings 1 Seniorities Junior (Analyst/Associate, 2–4 yrs) Budget $60K USD gross/year 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role, including the NSFW note below. 🚫 NSFW comfort is the first gate on this screen. Our flagship product is an adult-content AI companionship platform — do not submit candidates unless comfort working on the business side of that has been explicitly confirmed on a call. ⛔️ Top Requirements NSFW: genuinely comfortable working on the business side of an adult-content product. Bachelor's degree in business, economics, engineering, finance, or another relevant quantitative field — no geography or institution requirement. Consulting background: Big4 or middle-tier consulting — Strategy or Operations practice, 2–4 years, still Analyst/Associate/Consultant level, not yet Senior. Strong analytical toolkit: structured problem solving, financial modeling (P&Ls, unit economics, ROI/payback logic), subscription-business metrics literacy (MRR/ARR, CAC, LTV, LTV:CAC ratio, retention/cohort analysis), and advanced Excel/Google Sheets (pivot tables, complex formulas, VLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH, sensitivity tables). Excellent communication + top-level English: distills complex analyses into crisp narratives for senior audiences — leads with the answer, then backs it up with evidence — and can independently build an executive-ready deck, not just fill in someone else's template. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For A hybrid analyst/operator seat — some weeks are spent modeling a decision, others are spent in the day-to-day of the business, unblocking processes and coordinating across teams. Works directly with the founders and exec team on strategy, operations, and growth — owns analyses end-to-end : scopes the question, pulls and interprets the data, and turns it into a recommendation, rather than primarily administrative reporting or passive dashboard maintenance. Builds financial models and KPI dashboards and runs special projects; uses Metabase and Excel daily (Metabase not required going in). Full task breakdown is in the candidate-facing JD. A high-visibility role for someone who wants the pace and breadth of consulting with the ownership of an operator, where they'll directly impact an AI product already used by 50M real users. Comfort with ambiguity and a bias for action: scopes their own work and drives it independently in a remote setting. At EverAI, that means working directly with founders and execs without the layers of a typical Big4 team — with direct exposure to the executive team and increasing scope and seniority as the company scales. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Analytical / structured problem solving — the core consulting skill. Can they list out the possible reasons behind a problem, say what data would prove or rule out each one, and work through it out loud? Financial modeling & business fluency — P&Ls, unit economics, ROI/payback logic, and subscription-business metrics literacy (MRR/ARR, CAC, LTV, LTV:CAC ratio, retention/cohort analysis). Data fluency — advanced Excel/Google Sheets (pivot tables, complex formulas, VLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH, sensitivity tables) is required. SQL, Python, or BI tooling are not required for this role — useful if present, not a gate. Ownership — can distinguish \"I built / analyzed / recommended\" from \"the team was responsible for\"; probe this on the business-problem walkthrough below. Communication — can independently build an executive-ready deck and manage a working relationship with a Manager or senior stakeholder; fully fluent, spoken and written. Education — Bachelor's degree in business, economics, engineering, finance, or another relevant quantitative field. No geography or institution attached to this requirement. Consulting-firm pedigree — see Target Company Pools below; tied directly to the Top Requirements consulting-background gate, not a loose sourcing preference. 🤖 AI usage is a positive signal for this role, not a hard requirement. Genuine curiosity about AI tools is a strong positive signal, but its absence is not disqualifying — unlike Ruby Engineer, Product Designer, Senior Product Manager, or AI Cinematic Video Editor, where it is mandatory. 📁 Target Company Pools Category Target companies Big4 (Strategy or Operations/Advisory practice only) Deloitte, PwC (incl. Strategy& — PwC's strategy practice, not a separate firm), EY, KPMG Middle-tier — elite boutique (same bar as Big4) Oliver Wyman, L.E.K., OC&C, Roland Berger, Kearney, Simon-Kucher 🏷️ Job titles to target — the entry/first-promotion titles across these firms: Analyst Business Analyst Associate Consultant Exact naming varies by firm (e.g. Deloitte: Analyst → Consultant; PwC/Kearney: Analyst → Associate → Senior Associate; EY/KPMG: Consultant → Senior Consultant) — screen for level, not the literal title string. Job titles to avoid — signal someone already past the Analyst/Associate band, too senior (and too expensive) for this seat even if the firm and tenure otherwise fit: Senior Consultant Senior Associate Engagement Manager Manager Principal, or anything above 🚩 Red Flags 🚫 Audit, Tax, M&A due diligence, or financial-advisory background — even at Big4, this is a different skillset entirely and doesn't transfer. McKinsey, BCG, or Bain (MBB) background, at any tenure — too expensive for this seat. Title already past the Analyst/Associate/Consultant band (Senior Consultant, Senior Associate, Engagement Manager, Manager, Principal+). Cannot explain personal contribution — relies on \"we\"/\"the team\" rather than a personal analysis or recommendation. Background is primarily administrative reporting or passive dashboard maintenance, with no evidence of independent analysis or interpretation. Vague or generic analytical examples that don't hold up to follow-up questions. Can't connect an analysis to an actual business decision or outcome. Claims fluency with a tool (Excel, financial modeling) but can't explain how they actually used it. NSFW comfort is hesitant. This is a Junior seat — do not reject for university geography, employer prestige outside the pools above, an unconventional path, or lack of Senior-level, company-wide strategic scope. Assess against the bar above, not against a Senior profile. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. Our flagship product is an adult-content AI companionship platform. Are you fully comfortable working on the business side of that day-to-day? What's the achievement from your current role you're most proud of? Why are you looking to leave consulting now? Walk me through a specific business problem you solved recently — what was the actual ask, what data you pulled, what you personally did, what you found, what you recommended, and what happened as a result? What tools do you actually use day to day for analysis (Excel/Sheets, anything else)? Walk me through how, not just what. Tell me about a time a client or stakeholder pushed back hard on your recommendation and you were sure you were right — what did you do? A client's revenue is declining 15% year-over-year. Walk me through how you'd approach figuring out why. How would you explain a complex analysis to someone with no data background? What are the top 2–3 things you're looking for in your next role? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: At least one promotion within the Analyst/Associate/Consultant band during their tenure. Not required on its own; if absent, explore why during screening (e.g. recent hire, firm's promotion cycle timing). Genuine curiosity about, or hands-on use of, AI tools. Exposure to tech, AI, or high-growth startup environments (companies/industries). 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Content Moderator Next → Past Briefs"},{"title":"Content Moderator — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"content-moderator.html","text":"Department Operations Team Legal Hiring Manager Maxwelle Sokol (Legal & Safety Lead) Location Asia preferred, particularly candidates in or near Philippines/Southeast Asia timezone, to strengthen global moderation coverage; elsewhere in Asia considered if working hours provide required coverage Openings 1 Seniorities Junior, Mid Budget Up to $20K USD/year 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (B2B, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role, including the daily explicit-content exposure and coverage requirements below. ⛔️ Top Requirements Daily explicit-content exposure: fully, unhesitatingly comfortable reviewing and discussing content depicting sexual themes, roleplay, and other adult content as the core of the day-to-day job — not occasional or incidental. Prior content moderation experience — for an online platform, reviewing real user-generated content at meaningful volume. Policy judgment — able to interpret and apply moderation guidelines with sound judgment on ambiguous/borderline cases, not just follow a checklist mechanically. Excellent English — including slang and nuanced communication; the job depends on correctly reading context and intent in user-generated content. Coverage: able to work the hours needed for global moderation coverage (see Location above). 🎯 What We Are Hiring For Sits on the Compliance Team. Day-to-day, works closely with the Senior Content Moderator; the function overall reports to Maxwelle Sokol (Legal & Safety Lead). Reviews and approves/rejects user-generated content (video, image, text) against platform standards, documenting the basis for each decision. Runs safety/compliance reviews on in-house content and workflows (e.g. datasets, AI characters). Acts on content flagged by internal detection systems, and tags/categorizes content for correct visibility across the platform. Our platform is an adult-content AI companionship product, so reviewing sexually explicit material and adult themes is a normal, core part of the daily workload — not an occasional exception. The profile: reviews content carefully, applies policy consistently, identifies violations/risk, makes judgment calls when content is ambiguous, escalates appropriately, works reliably at volume, and maintains quality/accuracy. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Moderation judgment — can follow policy, distinguish allowed vs. prohibited content, handle ambiguous/borderline cases, explain their reasoning, and escalate when appropriate. Attention to detail — concrete examples where accuracy and consistency mattered, ideally with real throughput/accuracy numbers. Reliability / operational execution — sustained accuracy and consistency at volume, not just a one-off good call. Communication — explains decisions clearly, reads context/slang/intent correctly, and raises or escalates issues appropriately. Coverage / working hours — Philippines/Southeast Asia preferred to strengthen global coverage; candidates elsewhere in Asia qualify if their working hours provide the same required coverage. This is a timezone/coverage need, not a nationality requirement. 🤖 AI usage is a positive signal for this role, not a hard requirement. Familiarity with AI tools is a strong positive signal, but its absence is not disqualifying — unlike Ruby Engineer, Product Designer, Senior Product Manager, or AI Cinematic Video Editor, where it is mandatory. 📁 Target Company Pools Tied directly to the Prior Content Moderation Experience requirement above — used to verify genuine, direct moderation experience rather than a generic customer-support seat. Category Target companies In-house — large consumer platforms (Trust & Safety) — real, direct exposure to moderation queues, policy enforcement, and escalation workflows at meaningful scale Meta, TikTok/ByteDance, Reddit, Discord, Twitch, Match Group. Much of this work is actually outsourced to a BPO vendor — confirm they were directly employed by the platform itself, not a contractor. In-house — adult content & AI companion platforms — direct, in-house content moderation experience on NSFW/adult content OnlyFans, Fansly, Chaturbate, Stripchat, ManyVids, LiveJasmin, Aylo/Mindgeek (past employees only), Replika, Character.AI, Chai. Confirm they were a direct employee of the platform, not a vendor/agency contractor placed there. Aylo/Mindgeek is off-limits for current employees only — past employees who've left are fine to approach (see Off-Limits Companies). LiveJasmin is handle-with-care — targeted outreach only for candidates with confirmed interest, never bulk/broad outreach. BPO / Trust & Safety outsourcing (Philippines & Asia) — a larger, more available pool, and often where this same work happens in practice — acceptable, but not the first choice given a direct in-house preference TaskUs, Teleperformance, Concentrix, Foundever, Sutherland, Alorica, WNS, iQor, Genpact. Confirm they worked an actual Trust & Safety/content-moderation queue, not a general customer-support seat at the same company. 🚩 Red Flags 🚫 Uncomfortable with daily explicit/NSFW exposure, or treats it as occasional/incidental rather than the core of the job. Claims direct Trust & Safety/platform experience that turns out to be a general customer-support seat, or a vendor/BPO placement rather than direct employment (see Target Company Pools above). Inconsistent application of policy/guidelines, or purely mechanical checklist-following with no judgment on ambiguous cases. Cannot explain the reasoning behind a past moderation decision, or gives vague/generic examples. Poor attention to detail — can't point to concrete accuracy/consistency evidence. Weak English comprehension of context, slang, or intent. Not comfortable with, or unable to commit to, the required working hours/coverage. Vague personal ownership in prior moderation/operational work — relies on \"the team\" rather than their own decisions. Do not reject a candidate merely for being outside the Philippines if their location and working hours satisfy the required coverage. Do not reject a BPO/outsourced Trust & Safety background outright — it's an accepted, if secondary, pool — provided the candidate demonstrates genuine queue experience and the judgment above. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. Our platform is an adult-content AI companionship product — you'd be reviewing and discussing sexually explicit material and adult themes daily, as the core of the job, not incidentally. Are you fully comfortable with that? Have you worked with sensitive content before — NSFW, or CSAM-adjacent detection/removal/DMCA work? (Not required — a bonus if so.) Establish genuine comfort with this through discussion — don't accept a generic \"yes, NSFW is fine\" without probing. What are you doing currently, and why are you considering a move? Walk me through your content moderation experience — what platform, what type of content, what volume, and what tools did you use? Tell me about a specific piece of borderline or ambiguous content you had to make a call on. How did you interpret the guideline, what did you personally decide, and how did you document it? Tell me about a time you disagreed with a guideline or a manager's call on a piece of content — what did you do? Give me an example where missing a small detail could have produced an incorrect outcome. What was your typical throughput and accuracy on that queue — roughly how many items per hour or per shift, and what was your error rate, if tracked? This work can be psychologically demanding over time. How do you personally manage exposure to disturbing content? What's your current location and timezone, and what are your typical working hours? Can you provide the coverage this role needs? Compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: Experience moderating adult content specifically, or handling DMCA/copyright issues. Fluency in additional languages. Familiarity with common moderation tools and automation platforms. Familiarity with AI tools — don't reject a candidate solely for lacking it. Adjacent backgrounds worth a look even without a literal \"content moderation\" title: Trust & Safety, platform/community operations, QA, fraud/risk operations, compliance operations, or customer/community support that regularly involved difficult content — these support but don't replace the Top Requirement of real user-generated-content review experience at volume. 💡 Sourcing tip: example of a strong profile for calibration — similar skill set, though this candidate is Senior level (this seat is Junior/Mid): this LinkedIn profile . Philippines/Southeast Asia is a priority sourcing pool because of the coverage need — not because of nationality. Qualification stays tied to working-hours coverage plus the capability bar above. 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Senior Product Manager Next → Business Analyst"},{"title":"Do's and Don'ts — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"dos-donts.html","text":"ℹ️ A quick reference for how we expect agency partners to operate. Following these keeps the process fast and the relationship strong. ✅ Do's Submit candidates exclusively through Ashby — never via email, LinkedIn, or WhatsApp Complete every field in the submission template before submitting @mention your TA contact in the notes field on every submission Confirm NSFW comfort explicitly before submitting — every time, every candidate Check the Open Roles page before submitting — only submit for roles marked ✅ Open Check the country coverage table before progressing a candidate in a non-standard location Check the Off-Limits Companies list before submitting current employees of restricted partners Include a recording link (with public sharing enabled) when the role or process requires a recorded screen Flag competing offers or active processes in the submission notes Be transparent with candidates about the NSFW nature of the product from the very first conversation Share the Candidate Handbook with every candidate before their first interview Reference our published salary range (in the JD / role brief) when discussing compensation with a candidate Share any feedback, ideas, market insights you have with the team, it's super helpful so we can collaborate better together! ❌ Don'ts Don't ask candidates for their current or past salary — our ranges are already published in the JD, so this is no longer needed and no longer allowed Don't contact Hiring Managers directly — all communication goes through TA, unless explicitly stated otherwise Don't submit the same candidate to multiple roles without flagging it Don't submit speculatively for roles that are paused or not listed as open Don't submit candidates who require visa sponsorship — we do not sponsor Don't submit candidates from blocked countries or currently employed at off-limits companies Don't re-submit a previously rejected candidate without checking with your TA contact first Don't send volume over quality — three weak profiles damage your standing more than one strong one helps Don't promise candidates a specific timeline or outcome — that's for TA to communicate Don't hide or downplay the NSFW nature of the product to get a candidate through the door ← Previous Hiring Process Next → Pitching the Company"},{"title":"Engineering at EverAI — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"engineering.html","text":"If you're evaluating a role here, you deserve a clear picture of what you'd actually be working on . This section gives you a direct, honest look at what Engineering at EverAI actually looks like: Under the Hood covers our infrastructure, stack, and scale — the technical reality of what you'd be working on from day one. The EverAI Way: What Shipping Fast Really Means covers how we work — our engineering culture, decision-making principles, and what we expect from everyone on the team. ← Previous Safety and Ethics Next → Under the Hood"},{"title":"The EverAI Way — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"everai-way.html","text":"The EverAI Way: What Shipping Fast Really Means At EverAI, speed matters. We move fast because it helps us learn faster, validate ideas earlier, and stay ahead. We move fast because speed is a competitive advantage. Shipping fast does not mean rushing or lowering the bar. It means focusing on the right problem, keeping solutions simple, and reducing wasted time. We value small, safe, high-leverage changes that are easy to review, test, and improve. We care more about proving something that works than overbuilding too early. The goal is to find the simplest way to create value now, then iterate from there. Speed also comes from communication. Strong teams flag risks early, ask for help quickly, and keep others informed so work keeps moving. In practice, shipping fast at EverAI means: solving the right problem first starting with the simplest effective solution keeping scope tight communicating early and clearly improving quality as we go That's how we move with urgency without losing quality. ← Previous Under the Hood Next → Why Join Us?"},{"title":"Get in Touch — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"get-in-touch.html","text":"We're looking for exceptional talent ready to ship & scale world-first AI products fast, and co-create with us this category defining business. Explore our open roles and see where you can make an impact. If you're passionate about creating the future of AI and want to join our team, we want to meet you! 👉 Check out here our open roles and apply Or, if you're curious about what we're up to , visit our socials: Our Website Our LinkedIn Page Our Glassdoor Page ← Previous Our Recruitment Process Next → Applicant Privacy Notice"},{"title":"EverAI Candidate Handbook","url":"handbook.html","text":"👋 Welcome! Hey there! Thanks for checking out EverAI. This handbook was made just for you, a potential new colleague, to give you a sneak peek into who we are, what drives us, and how we collaborate to make big things happen. We're super excited that you're considering joining our team, and we can't wait to see what we can create together! Check out the pages below to learn more about us! 🚨 Newsflash 🗞️ : Candy.ai, EverAI's flagship product, is now the 4th largest AI web product in the world by unique monthly users , under two years after launch. 👉 We have a real opportunity to shape entirely new categories and we need bright go-getters to help us make this happen . 👉 If that excites you… dive into this handbook, prepare well for your interviews and LET'S GOOOOO ! 🔥 🚧 Our team is working on building more candidate resources. If you don't see what you're looking for, please feel free to reach out to your recruiter anytime. We're your partners in this journey, and we're here to answer any questions you may have along the way! :) Table of contents 👥 Who We Are ↗ 💻 What We Do ↗ 🛡️ Safety and Ethics ↗ ⚙️ Engineering at EverAI ↗ 🚧 Under the Hood (part of Engineering at EverAI) ↗ ⚡ The EverAI Way (part of Engineering at EverAI) ↗ 🤔 Why Join Us? ↗ 🏁 Our Recruitment Process ↗ 💬 Get in Touch ↗ 🔐 Applicant Privacy Notice ↗"},{"title":"Hiring Process — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"hiring-process.html","text":"Our Hiring Process ℹ️ We move fast, and strong candidates can progress through stages quickly. Your recruiter will guide you through any role-specific variations. 🔀 Hiring Process ℹ️ Ashby is the pipeline source of truth for every candidate. Submitting a candidate is a pre-screening / pipeline step , not a formal interview stage. Your TA contact owns recruiter screening and candidate communication, unless the role or process explicitly says otherwise. Role-specific pages override this default process where they say so. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer Pre-Screening — Submission & CV Review All candidates must be submitted via Ashby . When adding a candidate, you must @mention your TA contact in the notes and include the following template: Location / Timezone Visa / Right to Work LinkedIn Profile Portfolio or GitHub Salary Expectations Preferred Payment Currency Contract Type Availability Notice Period Other Active Processes Interview Recording Link Notes / Summary ➡️ Once submitted, your TA contact reviews the CV and notes in Ashby before recruiter screening. 1. Recruiter Screen — 30 min Owner: TA, unless the role or process explicitly says otherwise. A first conversation to confirm eligibility, motivation, and fit against the role brief and 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags . ⚠️ If any stage is recorded, always ask for the candidate's consent first. 2. Hiring Manager Interview — 30 min Owner: HM The first live interview with the role owner, focused on: Relevant experience Problem-solving approach Ownership and execution ability Alignment with the role scope 3. Case Study Owner: HM or team member (role dependent) Used to assess real-world working ability, quality of thinking, and how the candidate communicates and structures their work. Format and duration vary by role — see the role brief for specifics. Candidate receives an assignment (format depends on the role — e.g. a take-home brief or a live technical exercise) HM reviews the submission A follow-up debrief may take place 4. Final Interview / Cultural Fit — 30 min Owner: Leadership (typically CMO or CTO) A senior-level conversation focused on: Alignment with our working style Decision-making and ownership mindset Communication and collaboration 5. References Owner: HM or TA Reference checks are role and process dependent — your TA contact will confirm what's needed for a given role. There is no fixed universal number or required composition. 6. Offer Owner: TA Once all stages are complete: Compensation and contract terms are finalized internally Offer is presented to the candidate Contract and onboarding are handled through Deel, by our HR team Role-specific process deviations (see the relevant role brief) override this default. ✋ Before You Submit Candidates Before presenting EverAI to a candidate, make sure they understand what the company does. This is not a standard tech company. Candidates who aren't genuinely excited — or who are uncomfortable with the product — will not pass our process. Please share the Candidate Handbook with every candidate before submission. 🔴 The NSFW Conversation ⚠️ This must happen before every submission, without exception. Do not submit a candidate who has not been explicitly asked about this. EverAI's products involve sexually explicit AI content. Candidates will work or be exposed to NSFW material daily / weekly, depending on their role — whether in engineering, marketing, operations, or content roles. This is not incidental; it is central to the product. We are fully transparent about this from the very beginning of the process. We never hide it, and we are always upfront about it with every candidate. How to raise it: \"EverAI operates in the adult AI companionship space. This means working with explicit content. Have you thought about what that looks like in practice, and are you fully comfortable with it?\" If a candidate hesitates, it's usually better not to pursue and not to submit. ❌ ← Previous Our Open Roles Next → Do's and Don'ts"},{"title":"EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"index.html","text":"Topics 👋 How to Use Ashby ↗ 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags ↗ 📌 Our Open Roles ↗ ⏳ Hiring Process ↗ 🚦 Do's and Don'ts ↗ 🗣️ Pitching the Company ↗ 🆘 Preparing Candidates ↗ 🌐 Hiring Internationally ↗ ⚖️ Jurisdiction Risk Guide ↗ 🚫 Off-Limits Companies ↗ 🔖 Helpful Resources ↗"},{"title":"Hiring Internationally — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"international.html","text":"How and Where We Hire Internationally ℹ️ This page covers everything you need to know about how we engage talent globally — contract types, country coverage, blocked regions, and what to expect once an offer is accepted. 🌍 Types of Contracts for International Hiring We use Deel (deel.com) as our global hiring platform, allowing us to engage top talent in over 160 countries without requiring a local legal entity in every market. Depending on the country, we can engage candidates in one of two ways: EOR — Employer of Record Deel employs the candidate on our behalf. We cover employer social security contributions and statutory benefits as required by local law. Best for candidates who want or require local employment status. B2B — Contractor ➡️ Preferred The candidate operates as an independent contractor or through their own legal entity. No employer social security cost on our side. Best for candidates who are set up to work this way and where local regulations allow it. Our preference by default is B2B. Where costs are low or negligible, EOR or B2B are both viable. 🗺️ Our Hiring Preferences by Country The interactive table below shows every country where Deel operates, the type of contracts available, the employer social security cost, and our hiring preference for each. You can: 🔍 Search by country name 🔽 Filter by coverage type (EOR + Contractors / Contractors Only / EOR Only) 🔽 Filter by our preference (B2B Only / EOR or B2B / EOR) ↗ Open the full tool in a new tab ❌ Quick Reference — Blocked Countries Deel explicitly cannot operate in the following regions. Do not submit candidates based in these locations: 🚫 Afghanistan · Belarus · Cuba · Crimea (Ukraine) · Democratic Republic of Congo · Donetsk PR (Ukraine) · Iran · Iraq · Kherson Oblast (Ukraine) · Libya · Luhansk PR (Ukraine) · Myanmar · North Korea · Russia · Somalia · South Sudan · Sudan · Syria · Yemen · Zaporizhzhia Oblast (Ukraine) If a candidate is based in one of these regions, please flag it to your TA contact before investing time in the process. ‼️ Special Cases Malta: We have our own legal entity in Malta, so we operate EOR only through our own internal structure rather than a Deel EOR. ➡️ What You Need to Know Salary currency Candidates can receive payment in their local currency or USD/EUR, depending on their contract type and location. Confirm currency preference during screening and include it in the submission form — it helps us move faster at offer stage. Contract and onboarding Agencies are not involved in the contract or Deel setup. Once an offer is accepted, our TA and HR teams handle everything directly with the candidate through Deel. Typical onboarding setup takes 3–5 business days, so please set expectations with candidates accordingly — same-week starts are rarely possible. Right to work Always confirm a candidate's right to work and visa status before submission. Deel handles compliance in-country, but if a candidate requires sponsorship or has restrictions, flag it to your TA contact early. 🚫 For clarity: usually, we do not sponsor visas. ← Previous Preparing Candidates Next → Jurisdiction Risk Guide"},{"title":"Jurisdiction Risk Guide — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"jurisdiction.html","text":"🎯 Purpose This page is designed to help us distinguish in which countries it is legal vs. illegal to work for an adult content platform, and how that can impact candidates depending on where they live. We do not refuse to hire from any location — but we believe candidates deserve full transparency about the legal landscape so they can make an informed decision. The guide covers both traditional and AI-generated adult content, maps open positions to risk levels, and categorizes countries into three risk tiers. ⚠️ Important: This document does not constitute legal advice. It is a risk-flagging tool. Candidates in higher-risk jurisdictions should be encouraged to seek independent local legal counsel before accepting an offer. All parties should share the relevant risk information with candidates during the hiring process. 🪜 Tier Overview Tier Risk Level Candidate Disclosure Required Applies To 🔴 RED High criminal risk. Candidate must be informed that working for an adult content platform may expose them to criminal liability in their jurisdiction. Mandatory — full written risk disclosure before offer. All positions 🟡 YELLOW Partial or evolving risk. Laws may create exposure depending on role type. Enforcement varies. Mandatory — role-specific risk briefing before offer. Primarily content-facing roles 🟢 GREEN Low risk. Adult content is legal with standard regulatory compliance. Standard onboarding information. All positions 🔴 Red Tier Countries — High Risk (Mandatory Disclosure) These countries have outright bans on pornographic content (production, distribution, and/or possession). The laws typically cover all pornographic material regardless of medium, meaning AI-generated content is treated identically to filmed content . Candidates from these countries — even for non-content roles — may face criminal exposure simply by being employed by an adult content company. ⚠️ Action required: Before progressing any candidate from a Red tier country, you must provide them with a written risk disclosure (via email) explaining that employment with our platform could expose them to criminal liability under their local laws. Candidates must acknowledge this risk in writing (confirming via email) before an offer is extended. Middle East & Central Asia Saudi Arabia Iran Iraq Syria United Arab Emirates Qatar Kuwait Oman Bahrain Yemen Afghanistan Uzbekistan Turkmenistan Kazakhstan East & Southeast Asia China North Korea Indonesia Malaysia Thailand Cambodia Vietnam Laos Myanmar Brunei South Asia Pakistan Bangladesh Nepal Bhutan Maldives Africa Egypt Libya Somalia Sudan Ethiopia Eritrea Uganda Tanzania Burkina Faso Botswana Algeria Equatorial Guinea Europe & Eurasia Belarus — Production, distribution, and promotion of pornographic materials punishable by up to 4 years imprisonment Armenia 🟡 Yellow Tier Countries — Moderate Risk (Role-Specific Disclosure) These countries have partial restrictions, evolving legislation, or broadly worded facilitation/promotion laws that may create risk depending on the specific role. Non-content roles generally carry lower exposure, but candidates should still be informed of the legal landscape. ⚠️ Action required: Provide candidates from Yellow tier countries with a role-specific risk briefing. For content-facing roles, the briefing should be equivalent to a Red tier disclosure. For non-content roles, a verbal briefing with written acknowledgment is sufficient. Europe Sweden — As of July 2025, purchasing live sexual content online is criminal (up to 1 year in prison). The law extends liability to anyone who facilitates or profits from such services. Pre-recorded content remains legal, but the broad \"facilitation\" language could potentially reach platform employees. Norway & Finland — Actively exploring legislation similar to Sweden's digital sex work ban. Monitor closely. Lithuania — Distribution and production of pornographic material is prohibited under criminal code. Ukraine — Production and distribution illegal; restrictions actively enforced. Turkey — Heavy internet censorship; pornography restricted and monitored. Bulgaria — Production and distribution of pornography is illegal. Asia South Korea — Online pornography is banned, though enforcement varies. Distribution is criminal. India — Complex obscenity laws; pornography distribution is illegal, but personal viewing is not explicitly banned. Publishing/transmitting obscene material online carries criminal penalties. Singapore — Viewing pornography online is technically illegal. Other Russia — Personal consumption allowed but unlicensed distribution is restricted. Morality laws are tightening. Papua New Guinea — Possession of pornography is illegal. 🟢 Green Tier Countries — Generally Safe These countries allow legal production and distribution of adult content involving consenting adults, subject to regulations such as age verification, record-keeping, and obscenity standards. All listed roles can generally be filled from these jurisdictions. United States (subject to federal and state regulations, including the TAKE IT DOWN Act and state-level age verification laws) Canada United Kingdom (Online Safety Act compliance required for platform operations) Germany France (age verification requirements enforced by ARCOM) Netherlands Spain Italy Portugal Czech Republic Hungary Romania Poland Austria Belgium Ireland Denmark Australia (age verification for social media; adult content regulated but legal) New Zealand Japan (legal with censorship requirements) Israel Taiwan Most of Latin America (Argentina, Brazil, Mexico, Colombia, Chile, Peru, etc.) 🤖 AI-Generated Content — Special Considerations Since the platform produces AI-generated adult content, the following legal distinctions are important. AI content does NOT change country-level bans Countries that ban pornography ban all pornographic material regardless of production method. AI-generated content is treated identically to filmed content in ban countries. The \"no real people involved\" argument provides zero legal protection in Red tier jurisdictions. Non-consensual deepfakes are rapidly becoming illegal everywhere The US TAKE IT DOWN Act (May 2025) makes non-consensual AI-generated intimate images a federal felony. The UK Data (Use and Access) Act 2025 criminalizes even creating such images. The EU violence against women directive addresses this at the European level. This applies even in Green tier countries. AI-generated CSAM is universally illegal Illegal under US federal law and the laws of 45+ states, with massive increases in enforcement. Universally criminal across the EU, UK, and virtually all jurisdictions. Internal CSAM prevention guidelines are essential for compliance. Fully synthetic content (fictional characters) is a legal gray area In most US states, fully synthetic AI adult content depicting no real person is not explicitly illegal but may be subject to general obscenity laws. However, this space is evolving rapidly — in 2026, legislators are expected to broaden laws to cover AI platforms, payment processors, and hosting providers. The Compliance Associate should monitor this actively. Platform compliance obligations in Green countries Even in permissive jurisdictions, AI adult content platforms face growing requirements around age verification (UK, France, Germany, Italy, Spain, multiple US states), content labeling (EU AI Act transparency obligations), takedown procedures (TAKE IT DOWN Act — 48-hour removal requirement by May 2026), and record-keeping. ✅ Our Recommendations Always disclose jurisdiction risk to candidates*. We do not block hiring from any location, but transparency is non-negotiable. Candidates deserve to understand the legal environment before they commit. For Red tier countries, provide a full written risk disclosure and obtain written acknowledgment from the candidate before progressing to offer stage. We strongly recommend that candidates in these jurisdictions seek independent legal advice at their own discretion. For Yellow tier countries, tailor the disclosure to the role. Content-facing roles warrant a full written disclosure. Non-content roles warrant at minimum a verbal briefing with written acknowledgment. Prioritize candidates from Green tier countries when possible. These jurisdictions have established legal frameworks for the adult content industry, which reduces friction for both the candidate and the company. Monitor Sweden, Norway, and Finland closely. Sweden's 2025 law set a precedent that others may follow; the \"facilitation\" language is broad enough to potentially affect platform employees. Flag this proactively to candidates from these countries. Engage our Compliance Associate early if you're unsure about a specific jurisdiction or role combination. They can provide additional guidance. Keep records of all risk disclosures and candidate acknowledgments. This protects the candidate, the agency, and our company. *This disclosure applies at time of hire; candidates should notify HR if they relocate. ℹ️ This document was prepared in April 2026 and updated in May 2026 based on publicly available legal information. Laws in this space change rapidly. All parties should always encourage candidates in restricted jurisdictions to verify current regulations with qualified local legal counsel. This guide is a risk-flagging tool, not a legal opinion. ← Previous Hiring Internationally Next → Off-Limits Companies"},{"title":"Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"lifecycle-marketer.html","text":"Department Growth Hiring Manager Thomas Lacroix, Co-founder & CMO Location Worldwide Openings 1 Seniorities Senior Budget €90K–€100K + bonus 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role. ⛔️ Top Requirements Owns meaningful lifecycle areas, not only newsletters/sends. Can show commercial impact on purchase, retention, revenue or LTV. Understands incrementality and can explain how impact was proven. Remains hands-on with journeys, segmentation, testing and analysis. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For The Opportunity: the ambition is to establish CRM as a major revenue channel. See 🗣️ Pitching the Company for company scale and growth context. Primary focus of the role: registered-user-to-first-purchase conversion, token revenue, and repeat token purchase frequency. Broader ownership: onboarding, retention, churn prevention, reactivation, and LTV. The Team: This is a headcount increase, not a replacement. The existing CRM team brings strong operational and deliverability expertise. This hire will add stronger conversion, experimentation, and monetization leadership. Reporting Line: Reports directly to Thomas Lacroix, Co-founder and CMO. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Owns meaningful parts of the lifecycle, not just newsletters or sends. Can show commercial impact on purchase, retention, revenue or LTV. Understands incrementality and can explain how impact was proven. Is still hands-on with journeys, segmentation, testing and analysis. Also confirms relevant B2C experience at scale (a high-volume consumer business built around subscriptions, repeat deposits, tokens, credits, virtual currency, or another recurring-purchase model where CRM directly influenced revenue), and ownership/problem-solving without a finished playbook. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Mostly campaign execution with no lifecycle ownership. Only engagement metrics. Strategy/management only; execution sits elsewhere. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move? What attracted you to EverAI and this opportunity? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook — how deeply did you explore the product? Are you fully comfortable working with uncensored models and adult-oriented content? In your current or most recent role, what were your actual CRM goals and primary success metrics? What is the most significant CRM achievement you personally delivered, ideally within the past 6–12 months? What did you personally change, and what measurable business impact did it have? How did you measure that impact, and how did you establish that CRM — not another factor — caused it? Did you use holdouts, control groups, or another incrementality method? Which channels, CRM platforms, segmentation logic, and campaign workflows do you personally manage? Which business KPIs do you directly own? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three companies? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance ✨ Strong Additional Signals Increased CRM from a minor channel into a meaningful revenue contributor Built or significantly redesigned a CRM function Experience in iGaming, free-to-play gaming, or another repeat-purchase model Experience leading or coaching CRM specialists Uses AI for analysis, segmentation, personalization, experimentation, or content development ⚠️ Target companies are a sourcing aid, not proof of qualification. 📁 Primary Industries Based on our successful hires, confirmed by leadership, or a direct strategic match. Industry Target companies iGaming and Online Betting — Closest match for first-purchase conversion, repeat deposits, promotions, retention, reactivation, and LTV Flutter Entertainment, PokerStars, Betfair, Sisal, Adjarabet, Betsson Group, LeoVegas, Entain, Kaizen Gaming, Superbet, ComeOn Group, Tipico, FDJ United, evoke/888, Casumo, Gaming Innovation Group Free-to-Play and Social Gaming — Strong match for virtual currencies, repeat purchases, personalized offers, player retention, and experimentation Playtika, Moon Active, King, Supercell, Scopely, Product Madness, Homa Games, Voodoo, Miniclip, Socialpoint, Wooga, SuperPlay, Stillfront Group 📁 Secondary Industries Also worth sourcing from. Industry Target companies Consumer Subscription Products — Strong for onboarding, free-to-paid conversion, churn reduction, retention, and LTV Flo Health, Welltech, Freeletics, Blinkist, Babbel, Headspace, Calm, Strava, Komoot, Nord Security, Surfshark, Proton, Fabulous 📁 Selective Industries Relevant only in specific conditions — treat with more scrutiny. Industry Target companies High-Frequency E-Commerce and Marketplaces — Relevant when CRM is automated, behavioral, personalized, and directly accountable for repeat revenue Vinted, Zalando, HelloFresh, Delivery Hero, Wolt, Bolt, Glovo, GetYourGuide, Omio, Flix, Rohlik Group, Otrium 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Senior Affiliate Manager Next → Senior Product Manager"},{"title":"Off-Limits Companies — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"off-limits.html","text":"ℹ️ Due to ongoing partnerships and relationships, certain companies are off-limits for active recruitment. This applies to current employees only — past employees who no longer work at these companies can be contacted freely. Any exception requires explicit approval from Alexis (CEO) before outreach. 🛑 Do Not Recruit From Current employees at the following companies must not be approached : Aylo Nutaku Mindgeek Traffic Stars Advidi Ovation (related to Advidi) XVideos xHamster Traffic Junky Twinred Pika KlingAI Admaze 🚨 Docler / Byborg / LiveJasmin — handle with care Targeted outreach to specific individuals is permitted, particularly those we have previously confirmed interest in. Do not broadly contact or send bulk outreach to people from these organizations. We want to maintain a positive relationship with this company. If a strong candidate emerges organically, we are open to moving forward — but tread carefully. ← Previous Jurisdiction Risk Guide Next → Helpful Resources"},{"title":"Our Open Roles — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"open-roles.html","text":"Our Open Roles (+ Briefs & Pre-Screen Questions) 🚩 Before reviewing any role: read the shared Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags guide. These rules apply across EverAI unless the role brief explicitly says otherwise. ℹ️ This page lists all roles we are actively hiring for at EverAI — the company behind Candy.ai , one of the leading AI companion platforms in the adult space. We work with a select group of agency partners to source talent across R&D, Growth, and Operations. Before submitting candidates, make sure you have read this guide. 🎯 How to Approach Submissions Quality > Volume: One perfectly matched candidate is worth more to us than ten \"maybe\" profiles. Check the Off-Limits List: Ensure your candidates are not currently employed by our restricted partners, on this list here . If unsure whether a candidate is a fit, ask your TA contact before submitting ✋ Submission Quality Bar ℹ️ IMPORTANT We strongly prefer fewer, high-quality candidates over volume. Before clicking \"Submit\" in Ashby , run every candidate through this final checklist: The \"Doer\" Test: Does this person actually build things, or do they just \"manage\" processes? We only hire hands-on executors. Budget Alignment: Are they strictly within the ranges listed in the table below? Location & Deel Logic: Does their location align with our B2B vs. EOR preference? (Check this page before submitting). NSFW Comfort: Have you explicitly confirmed they are comfortable working for an adult / explicit-content product? Direct exposure frequency is role-specific — see the role brief and 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags . ❌ If the answer to any of the above is no → do not submit. ➡️ Open Roles by Department ℹ️ To access a role's full brief and pre-screen questions, click the role name below. Each department also has its own routing page: Growth , R&D , Operations . R&D Role Seniority Openings Location / Timezone Budget Status Product Designer Senior 2 Europe €80K–€100K (up to €120K exceptional) ✅ Open Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer Senior 2 Europe (CET ±3) ~€100K (up to €120K exceptional) ✅ Open Security Engineer Mid or Senior 1 Europe (CET overlap 80%) Mid: €65K–€85K Senior: €85K–€115K ✅ Open Senior Product Manager Senior 2 Europe Up to €120K ✅ Open AI Cinematic Video Editor Mid or Senior 10 Worldwide (CET overlap not required); not actively sourcing US/Canada Mid: LATAM $28K–$42K · Europe €42K–€60K Senior: LATAM $42K–$58K · Europe €60K–€73K US: up to $95K USD for an exceptional candidate ✅ Open Growth Role Seniority Openings Location / Timezone Budget Status Performance Marketer ↳ Jr Adult RTB · Sr Adult RTB · Jr Mainstream · Sr Mainstream Junior - Senior 4 Worldwide €42K (Junior) · €70K–€100K total package (Senior) ✅ Open Senior Affiliate Manager Senior 1 Europe $70K–$80K USD base ✅ Open Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager Senior 1 Worldwide €90K–€100K + bonus ✅ Open Operations Role Seniority Openings Location / Timezone Budget Status Content Moderator Junior, Mid 1 Asia preferred (Philippines / SEA timezone strongest fit) Up to $20K USD/year ✅ Open Business Analyst Junior 1 Worldwide. Asia or Europe preferred. $60K USD gross/year ✅ Open 💰 Salary ranges are published in our Job Descriptions — current salary questions are off the table. All of our budget ranges are listed above and in the role briefs and JDs. Since the range is already public, we can no longer ask candidates about their current or past salary — anchor the conversation on our published range and their expectations against it instead. ➡️ Role Briefs ℹ️ These briefs cover everything you need to source and screen candidates correctly before submission. Read it in full before sending profiles. Performance Marketer ↗ Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer ↗ AI Cinematic Video Editor ↗ Product Designer ↗ Security Engineer ↗ Senior Affiliate Manager ↗ Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager ↗ Senior Product Manager ↗ Content Moderator ↗ Business Analyst ↗ Past Briefs (not currently open) ↗ ← Previous Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags Next → Hiring Process"},{"title":"Past Briefs","url":"past-briefs.html","text":"Closed roles 🤖 AI LLM Tech Lead ↗ 📹 AI Marketing Video Editor ↗ ⚖️ AI Legal Specialist ↗"},{"title":"Junior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"performance-marketer-junior-adult-rtb.html","text":"Department Growth Hiring Manager Egor Location Worldwide Openings 1 Seniorities Junior Track Adult RTB Explicit creatives Direct exposure required Budget €42K 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role. ⛔️ Top Requirements Direct campaign/platform exposure. Understanding of traffic/performance metrics. Ability to explain personal actions and results. Comfort working with Adult / explicit-content acquisition. 🎯 Role Mission Operate and optimize acquisition campaigns across adult, native, push and RTB traffic sources. The person will make evidence-based campaign decisions and progressively take ownership of larger budgets. 📋 Responsibilities Launch and optimize adult acquisition campaigns. Monitor performance by traffic source, placement, format, market and creative. Reallocate spend based on CPA, conversion and traffic quality. Identify weak placements, fraud and low-quality traffic. Contribute to creative hypotheses and testing plans. Evaluate performance beyond clicks and registrations. Analyze subscription conversion and customer quality. Maintain accurate campaign tracking and reporting. Communicate results and recommended actions clearly. Develop toward independent ownership of substantial campaign budgets. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Has direct campaign exposure and works inside the ad platforms. Understands core metrics and can connect them to actions. Can separate their own contribution from the wider team. Shows learning speed and creative/testing curiosity. There is no fixed minimum budget for Junior candidates. The candidate must still prove real execution and decision ownership. Do not apply the Senior $300K/month spend bar to Junior candidates — the spend question establishes level of ownership and exposure, not a hard minimum. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Only reporting/coordinating while others execute. Recites metrics but cannot explain what action they took. Only gives team results. Experience is mainly account management, partnerships or publisher monetization. Cannot explain how traffic quality was evaluated; reasoning stops at clicks or CTR. No meaningful involvement in creative testing. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What did you notice, and how far did you test the product? Are you fully comfortable working with explicit content as part of your day-to-day role? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role at [company], what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest growth / technical achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? What was the actual performance metric, and was it a company goal? Which platforms do you personally manage today, and what monthly budget do you directly control? If unclear: How much of that do you personally touch vs. the wider team? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Track-Specific Guidance Target profiles should show: Direct RTB/native/push buying. Campaign setup and optimization. Tracking/postbacks. Traffic-quality analysis. Creative testing involvement. Relevant platforms and tools include TrafficJunky, ExoClick, TrafficStars, Clickadu, PropellerAds, Adsterra, TrafficFactory, Taboola, Outbrain, MGID, Voluum, Binom, RedTrack, and server-to-server postbacks/sub-ID/placement-level tracking. Direct experience with every platform is not required. Experience at an adult advertising network, publisher or adtech company is relevant only when the candidate personally bought and optimized traffic from the advertiser side. 📁 Sourcing Guidance ⚠️ TrafficJunky and TrafficStars are Off-Limits Companies. This applies to candidates currently employed by those networks — not to candidates who simply bought traffic on their platforms as an advertiser. Do not approach current employees of TrafficJunky or TrafficStars for this or any role; see the Off-Limits Companies page. 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer Next → Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB"},{"title":"Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"performance-marketer-junior-mainstream.html","text":"Department Growth Hiring Manager Thomas Lacroix (CMO & Co-founder) Location Worldwide Openings 1 Seniorities Junior Track Mainstream Explicit creatives Not handled directly NSFW product comfort Required Budget €42K 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role. ⛔️ Top Requirements Direct, hands-on campaign execution. Understanding of core acquisition metrics. Ability to explain personal contribution. Testing/creative curiosity and learning speed. 🎯 Role Mission Operate and optimize mainstream paid-acquisition campaigns while developing the analytical, creative and commercial judgment required to own larger budgets. 📋 Responsibilities Launch and optimize campaigns on mainstream platforms. Monitor performance by campaign, audience, market and creative. Reallocate spend based on conversion and commercial performance. Contribute to creative hypotheses and testing plans. Identify weak performance and recommend actions. Analyze CAC, ROAS, conversion and cohort quality. Maintain accurate tracking and reporting. Communicate findings and decisions clearly. Develop toward independent ownership of larger budgets. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Has direct campaign exposure and works inside the platforms. Understands core metrics and can connect them to actions. Can separate their own contribution from the team's. Shows learning speed and some testing/creative curiosity. There is no fixed minimum budget for Junior candidates. The candidate must still demonstrate real operating responsibility. Do not apply the Senior $300K/month spend bar to Junior candidates — the spend question establishes level of ownership and exposure, not a hard minimum. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Only reporting/coordinating while others execute. Recites metrics but cannot explain what action they took. Only gives team results. Experience is mainly B2B lead generation, ABM or SaaS demand generation. Cannot connect campaign metrics to a business outcome. Creative involvement was administrative; knowledge is based mainly on certifications or coursework. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What did you notice, and how far did you test the product? Are you fully comfortable working with explicit content as part of your day-to-day role? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role at [company], what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest growth / technical achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? What was the actual performance metric, and was it a company goal? Which platforms do you personally manage today, and what monthly budget do you directly control? If unclear: How much of that do you personally touch vs. the wider team? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Track-Specific Guidance Target profiles should show: Direct paid social / UA execution. Meta / TikTok / Google or similar platforms. Mobile gaming, subscription apps, DTC, dating/social, or agency backgrounds can all be relevant. Hands-on campaign operation is mandatory. Relevant channels include Meta, TikTok, Google, Instagram, Reddit, and other scalable consumer-acquisition platforms. Candidates do not need experience with every platform — they must demonstrate direct execution on at least one relevant acquisition channel. 📁 Sourcing Guidance ⚠️ Important: A target company is only a sourcing signal. It is not evidence of fit . Every candidate must still pass the screening criteria above. Tier 1 — start sourcing here Industry Target companies Mobile Gaming Playtika, Scopely, Zynga, Product Madness, Socialpoint, Tactile Games, Voodoo, King, Homa Games, Vizor, MWM, Wooga, Moon Active, PLAYSTUDIOS, Huuuge Games, Bagelcode, Sandsoft Games, Netmarble, AppLovin, Gameloft, Ubisoft VPN / Privacy / Security Subscriptions Kape Technologies, CyberGhost, ExpressVPN, NordVPN / Nord Security, Clario, Avast / HMA, MacPaw / MacKeeper Dating / Social Discovery Social Discovery Group, Taimi, Tinder, Hily, Badoo, HER, Match Group / Meetic, Together Networks, SKELAR, Wizz, Timeleft, Tango High-scale Consumer Subscription Apps BetterMe, Gismart, Picsart, Bending Spoons, Pocket FM, MasterClass, Flo, Appflame, DataCamp Tier 2 — strong adjacent pools Category Target companies Performance-first DTC / Subscription Brands HelloFresh / Factor, Trafilea, Lume, Ritual, AG1, Adore Me, True Classic, MANUAL Performance / Mobile Growth Agencies Candidate must personally buy media and be able to isolate their own spend, decisions and results. Portfolio/client totals do not count. Addict Mobile, Moburst, ConsultMyApp, AppAgent, PPC AdWise Conditional — only submit if screening criteria are clearly met Category Target companies Fintech Revolut Telehealth / Femtech Ro, Maven Clinic, Eucalyptus, ZAVA, Thirty Madison, Clue, Evvy, BlueChew, Willow, Heidi, Koala®, Everlab, Pilot, hims & hers Broader E-Commerce No company whitelist — qualify on profile evidence. General Consumer Subscription Apps Duolingo, Lightricks, Sleep Cycle, Rise Science, Hallow, Fastic, Kaspersky, Noom, Numan, Inkitt, DramaBox, NetShort, DramaWave, Beijing Dianzhong Technology, Lingokids, sofatutor, ŌURA Dating / Social Discovery — adjacent, inconsistent evidence Yubo, Smitten 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB Next → Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream"},{"title":"Recruiter Screening Guide — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"performance-marketer-screening-guide.html","text":"Performance Marketer — Recruiter Screening Guide ℹ️ Purpose: use the first interview to determine whether the candidate has the hands-on performance marketing experience, measurable achievements, motivation, and communication skills required to progress. Applies the same way across all four tracks. Include a summary of answers in your submission notes in Ashby. ⛔️ Senior Performance Marketer 💡 The $300K+/month spend bar is Mainstream-specific. For Adult RTB, adapt the budget question to the candidate's actual buying model (flat deals, direct deals, partnership-driven traffic) rather than mechanically enforcing $300K — see the Senior Adult RTB brief . Screening criteria Is personally running and optimizing campaigns now. Personally controls or drives meaningful acquisition commercially; Mainstream target is $300K+/month, Adult RTB is evaluated on deal/relationship model instead (see above). Can show recent measurable commercial impact. Personally participates in creative testing and iteration. Red flags Team/company spend presented as personal spend. Vague \"performance improved\" with no numbers. No current hands-on execution. Creative entirely owned by another team. Questions What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What did you notice, and how far did you test the product? Are you fully comfortable working with explicit content as part of your day-to-day role? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role at [company], what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest growth / technical achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? What was the actual performance metric? Was it a company goal? Which platforms do you personally manage today, and what monthly budget do you directly control? If unclear: How much of that is personally yours vs. team / portfolio / company spend? Walk me through your creative-testing process. What decisions do you personally make? How do you decide what to scale or kill? Give me one recent example where you changed spend or campaign strategy based on CAC / CPA / ROAS / LTV / payback. What did you change? What happened? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? ⚠️ Senior Mainstream candidates should not progress if personal spend ownership cannot be verified at approximately $300K+/month. For Senior Adult RTB, do not apply this fixed number — the equivalent bar is verified commercial control through platform spend, flat/direct deals, or partnership-driven traffic. For any track, do not progress if execution is delegated rather than current and hands-on. ⛔️ Junior Performance Marketer Screening criteria Has direct campaign exposure and works inside the platforms. Understands core metrics and can connect them to actions. Can separate their own contribution from the team's. Shows learning speed and some testing/creative curiosity. Red flags Only reporting/coordinating while others execute. Recites metrics but cannot explain what action they took. Only gives team results. Questions What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What did you notice, and how far did you test the product? Are you fully comfortable working with explicit content as part of your day-to-day role? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role at [company], what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest growth / technical achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? What was the actual performance metric, and was it a company goal? Which platforms do you personally manage today, and what monthly budget do you directly control? If unclear: How much of that do you personally touch vs. the wider team? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? ⚠️ Do not apply the Senior $300K/month spend threshold to Junior. For Junior, the spend question establishes level of ownership and exposure, not a hard minimum. 📖 Glossary Personally managed budget Budget the candidate directly controls and optimizes, not total team, portfolio, or company spend. Hands-on The candidate personally executes in the relevant platform/tool, not only manages a team, agency, or strategy. Ownership What the candidate personally did, decided, changed, or delivered versus what the wider team/company achieved. Commercial impact Measurable effect on revenue, CAC/CPA, ROAS, LTV, retention, purchase rate, or another core business KPI. Mainstream vs Adult RTB The Performance Marketing tracks differ by traffic environment; always confirm which track the candidate is relevant for. 🚩 Classify every large number on a CV — don't take it at face value. A large \"portfolio\" or \"budget\" figure can be supply-side revenue, stale, or account-manager-driven rather than personally controlled acquisition spend. 📖 Vocabulary Cheat Sheet Positive signal for the RTB tracks (Junior or Senior) if you see these on a CV: Adult and RTB networks: TrafficJunky, TrafficStars, ExoClick, Clickadu, PropellerAds, Adsterra, Adnium, TrafficFactory, EroAdvertising Native and push: Taboola, Outbrain, MGID, Revcontent Also relevant: Reddit Ads (a live channel for us), popunder / in-page push / native / display formats Tracking and attribution: Voluum, Binom, RedTrack, S2S postbacks, sub-ID structures, click ID, DOI, Everflow, Impact, getCAKE, Cellxpert, AppsFlyer Metrics that signal depth: CPA, blended CPA, FTD, rebill, DOI-to-subscription, cohort payback, LTV/CAC, traffic source quality, fraud detection Mainstream-only stack — neutral to negative for the RTB tracks: Google Ads/PMax/Demand Gen, Meta Ads Manager only, SA360, DV360, LinkedIn Ads, Criteo, Amazon Ads, Klaviyo, HubSpot, Braze, Salesforce Marketing Cloud. These are exactly what we want for the Mainstream tracks — the distinction is which track the candidate is being screened against. ← Previous Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream"},{"title":"Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"performance-marketer-senior-adult-rtb.html","text":"Department Growth Hiring Manager Hugo Location Worldwide Openings 1 Seniorities Senior Track Adult RTB Explicit creatives Direct exposure required Budget €70K–€100K total package 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role. ⛔️ Top Requirements Hands-on media buying / acquisition ownership. Adult RTB / native / push — or strongly comparable restricted/aggressive acquisition mechanics. Clear, measurable commercial impact. Direct optimisation ownership. Seniority evaluated through traffic/deal/platform/economics scope — not a fixed $300K/month spend gate. 🎯 Role Mission Own and scale adult acquisition at significant spend while protecting profitability, subscription quality and long-term customer value. 📋 Responsibilities Own adult acquisition campaigns end to end. Control and reallocate substantial campaign budgets. Scale profitable traffic sources, placements and creatives. Evaluate performance through CPA, rebill, LTV and payback. Diagnose tracking, fraud, placement and funnel problems. Build structured creative-testing systems. Define testing budgets, winner rules and stopping rules. Guide creative production using performance evidence. Identify new traffic sources and expansion opportunities. Communicate strategy, decisions, results and risks clearly. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Is personally running and optimizing campaigns now. Personally controls or drives meaningful acquisition commercially — via platform spend, flat/direct deals, publisher/network relationships, or partnership-driven traffic. Can show recent measurable commercial impact. Personally participates in creative testing and iteration. 💡 $300K+/month personally controlled spend is NOT a hard gate for this track. The Adult team works substantially through flat deals, direct deals, traffic-source relationships, publisher/network relationships, and partnership/business development — not only standard paid-media buying. Do not reject an excellent Adult candidate simply because they don't fit a standard monthly-spend model. Direct adult/RTB experience is strongly preferred but not mandatory . Candidates may also qualify from other sensitive/restricted/grey verticals — iGaming, casino, betting, dating, crypto, sweepstakes, nutra, or similar restricted-acquisition environments — where they show they understand harder acquisition environments and can operate commercially within them. Mainstream-only performance-marketing experience remains a weaker fit for this track. Also confirms current operating experience (still close to execution — strategy/advisory/account-management-only is not suitable), proven company experience at meaningful scale, personal campaign ownership, and product-category alignment (fully comfortable with uncensored products and explicit advertising creatives). 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Team/company spend presented as personal spend. Vague \"performance improved\" with no numbers. No current hands-on execution — direct media buying is no longer recent. Creative entirely owned by another team, or decisions depend entirely on account-manager recommendations. Profile is supply-side/publisher-side, or affiliate/account management without direct media buying. Profile is mainstream-only (Meta/Google/TikTok) with no meaningful RTB/native experience. Commercial reasoning stops at clicks or CTR; results cannot be personally attributed. Seniority masks distance from campaign execution. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What did you notice, and how far did you test the product? Are you fully comfortable working with explicit content as part of your day-to-day role? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role at [company], what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest growth / technical achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? What was the actual performance metric, and was it a company goal? Which platforms do you personally manage today, and what monthly budget or deal volume do you directly control? If unclear: How much of that is personally yours vs. team / portfolio / company spend? Walk me through your creative-testing process. What decisions do you personally make? How do you decide what to scale or kill? Give me one recent example where you changed spend or campaign strategy based on CAC / CPA / ROAS / LTV / payback. What did you change? What happened? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Track-Specific Guidance Priority profiles Adult / RTB / native media buyers iGaming / casino / betting performance teams Dating, crypto, sweepstakes, nutra, or similar restricted-acquisition profiles Mobile gaming candidates with genuine RTB/native/programmatic buying Performance agencies where the candidate personally buys media Strong signals (beyond spend): direct publisher/network relationships, negotiating flat or direct deals, partnership development, source-quality evaluation, commercial/funnel optimization, managing harder or restricted traffic. Advertiser-side buying across adult networks; native, push, display or popunder acquisition; placement-level optimization; traffic-quality and fraud analysis; rebill and subscription-economics experience; cohort analysis; flat-deal negotiation with publishers; international acquisition. Adult-industry or adtech experience without current advertiser-side execution is insufficient. Example of ideal/good candidate for calibration: this LinkedIn profile . 📁 Sourcing Guidance Relevant vocabulary (not a hard requirement — useful for recognizing genuine experience): TrafficJunky, TrafficStars, ExoClick, Clickadu, PropellerAds, Adsterra, EroAdvertising, TrafficFactory, Adnium, Voluum, Binom, RedTrack, S2S postbacks, sub-IDs, click IDs, CPA, FTD, cohort payback, LTV/CAC. 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Junior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB Next → Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream"},{"title":"Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"performance-marketer-senior-mainstream.html","text":"Department Growth Hiring Manager Thomas Lacroix (CMO & Co-founder) Location Worldwide Openings 1 Seniorities Senior Track Mainstream Explicit creatives Not handled directly NSFW product comfort Required Budget €70K–€100K total package 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role. ⛔️ Top Requirements Hands-on paid acquisition execution. $300K+/month personally controlled spend. Recent measurable commercial impact. Personal ownership of creative testing/iteration. Relevant B2C / consumer acquisition background. 🎯 Role Mission Own and scale mainstream paid acquisition across major consumer platforms while protecting CAC, LTV, payback and subscription profitability. 📋 Responsibilities Own campaigns across mainstream acquisition platforms. Control and reallocate substantial advertising budgets. Scale campaigns, audiences, markets and creatives. Improve CAC, ROAS, LTV, payback and subscription revenue. Diagnose performance changes across the advertising and product funnel. Build structured creative-testing programs. Establish testing budgets, winner rules and stopping rules. Work with creative teams to increase testing velocity. Navigate platform restrictions associated with sensitive products. Communicate commercial decisions and results clearly. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Is personally running and optimizing campaigns now. Personally controls meaningful spend — Senior Mainstream target is $300K+/month personally controlled. Can show recent measurable commercial impact. Personally participates in creative testing and iteration. Team budget, client portfolio value and company revenue do not count as personally managed spend unless the candidate personally controlled allocation and optimization. Years in marketing ≠ years in paid acquisition — general marketing, product marketing, partnerships, social media, account management, affiliate management, or demand generation do not count toward this bar unless the candidate personally operated acquisition campaigns. Also confirms current operating experience (still close to execution — strategy/advisory/account-management-only is not suitable), proven company experience at meaningful scale, personal campaign ownership, and product-category alignment (fully comfortable with uncensored products and explicit advertising creatives). 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Team/company/client portfolio numbers presented as personally controlled spend. Vague \"performance improved\" with no numbers. No current hands-on execution — has moved completely away from platform execution. Creative entirely owned by another team; cannot explain creative-testing logic. Execution is delegated to agencies or junior team members. Success is described only through platform metrics; seniority masks limited operating depth. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions What is your current situation, and why are you considering a move right now? What specifically attracted you to this opportunity with EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What did you notice, and how far did you test the product? Are you fully comfortable working with explicit content as part of your day-to-day role? Have you worked with NSFW or adult content in a professional context before? In your last role at [company], what were your actual goals, and what was the primary metric used to determine whether you were performing well? What is your biggest growth / technical achievement from the past 6–12 months? What measurable business impact did this achievement have? What was the actual performance metric? Was it a company goal? Which platforms do you personally manage today, and what monthly budget do you directly control? If unclear: How much of that is personally yours vs. team / portfolio / company spend? Walk me through your creative-testing process. What decisions do you personally make? How do you decide what to scale or kill? Give me one recent example where you changed spend or campaign strategy based on CAC / CPA / ROAS / LTV / payback. What did you change? What happened? What are your future career goals? Why did you leave each of your last two or three roles? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Track-Specific Guidance Strong signals: direct execution on Meta, TikTok, Google, Instagram or Reddit; multi-market acquisition; high-volume creative testing; consumer-subscription economics; experience scaling web funnels; experience navigating restrictions for sensitive products; cross-channel budget allocation. Named experience with Meta, TikTok, Google Ads/UAC, Snapchat, or native advertising; tracking/attribution experience (GA4, AppsFlyer, Adjust, Voluum); experience handling advertising restrictions, compliance issues or account bans. Example of ideal/good candidate for calibration: this LinkedIn profile . ✨ Preferred: $1M or more in personally controlled monthly spend; experience across multiple mainstream platforms; international or multi-market acquisition; high creative-testing velocity; experience with subscription funnels and cohort economics. 📁 Sourcing Guidance ⚠️ Important: A target company is only a sourcing signal. It is not evidence of fit . Every candidate must still pass the screening criteria above. Tier 1 — start sourcing here Industry Target companies Mobile Gaming Playtika, Scopely, Zynga, Product Madness, Socialpoint, Tactile Games, Voodoo, King, Homa Games, Vizor, MWM, Wooga, Moon Active, PLAYSTUDIOS, Huuuge Games, Bagelcode, Sandsoft Games, Netmarble, AppLovin, Gameloft, Ubisoft VPN / Privacy / Security Subscriptions Kape Technologies, CyberGhost, ExpressVPN, NordVPN / Nord Security, Clario, Avast / HMA, MacPaw / MacKeeper Dating / Social Discovery Social Discovery Group, Taimi, Tinder, Hily, Badoo, HER, Match Group / Meetic, Together Networks, SKELAR, Wizz, Timeleft, Tango High-scale Consumer Subscription Apps BetterMe, Gismart, Picsart, Bending Spoons, Pocket FM, MasterClass, Flo, Appflame, DataCamp Tier 2 — strong adjacent pools Category Target companies Performance-first DTC / Subscription Brands HelloFresh / Factor, Trafilea, Lume, Ritual, AG1, Adore Me, True Classic, MANUAL Performance / Mobile Growth Agencies Candidate must personally buy media and be able to isolate their own spend, decisions and results. Portfolio/client totals do not count. Addict Mobile, Moburst, ConsultMyApp, AppAgent, PPC AdWise Conditional — only submit if screening criteria are clearly met Category Target companies Fintech Revolut Telehealth / Femtech Ro, Maven Clinic, Eucalyptus, ZAVA, Thirty Madison, Clue, Evvy, BlueChew, Willow, Heidi, Koala®, Everlab, Pilot, hims & hers Broader E-Commerce No company whitelist — qualify on profile evidence. General Consumer Subscription Apps Duolingo, Lightricks, Sleep Cycle, Rise Science, Hallow, Fastic, Kaspersky, Noom, Numan, Inkitt, DramaBox, NetShort, DramaWave, Beijing Dianzhong Technology, Lingokids, sofatutor, ŌURA Dating / Social Discovery — adjacent, inconsistent evidence Yubo, Smitten 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream Next → Recruiter Screening Guide"},{"title":"Performance Marketer — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"performance-marketer.html","text":"📌 Open Roles We are hiring four Performance Marketers across two acquisition tracks and two seniority levels. Role Location Compensation Channel Junior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB Worldwide €42K Adult, native, push and RTB Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB Worldwide €70K–€100K total package Adult, native, push and RTB Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream Worldwide €42K Meta, TikTok, Google, Instagram and Reddit Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream Worldwide €70K–€100K total package Meta, TikTok, Google, Instagram and Reddit ⚠️ Always use the exact track brief below. Requirements and sourcing guidance differ by track; do not apply requirements from one track to another. 🎯 The Two Tracks Adult RTB — adult/native/push/RTB acquisition environments. Junior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB Mainstream — Meta/TikTok/Google/other mainstream paid acquisition environments. Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream ➡️ Role-Specific Briefs Junior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB ↗ Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB ↗ Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream ↗ Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream ↗ Recruiter Screening Guide ↗ Next → Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer"},{"title":"Pitching the Company — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"pitch.html","text":"How to Pitch the Company to Candidates ℹ️ Use this page to introduce EverAI to candidates clearly and honestly. The goal is to attract people who are genuinely excited — not to oversell. 🍭 About EverAI Use these talking points when introducing the company to a candidate. The headline EverAI is the company behind Candy.ai — one of the leading AI companion platforms in the world. Candy.ai is currently the 4th largest AI web product globally by unique monthly users, started in 2023. The scale 50 million users and counting Nine-figure annualized revenue $10M in seed funding Goal: 100M users in the next 12 months, 500M beyond that The product AI companionship: users design and interact with AI characters through text, AI phone calls, image and video generation, and a memory system that builds long-term context The product operates in the NSFW/adult content space — this is core to the business and must be raised clearly with every candidate before they proceed The team Fully remote, ~100 people, worldwide , most coming from Tier 1 tech companies Co-founded by Thomas Lacroix (CMO, ex-Curatible/MTK Digital) and Michael Monin (CTO, ex-MTK Digital/Zipchat) The founding team has a proven track record of building and scaling products to IPO The opportunity This is genuinely rare: a fast-growing, profitable, AI-first company with real traction, a category-defining product, and a founding team that has done it before Candidates joining now will have direct impact and grow with the company as it scales to hundreds of millions of users What's coming next AI Live Streaming — an industry first, currently in development AI chat in 16+ languages AR/VR integration Improved AI-generated video (currently 10s, with significant room to grow) Global expansion and reaching 100M users, just with CandyAI Why candidates join Real ownership and impact from day one — no layers, no bureaucracy, and a flat hierarchy Fast career progression as the company scales aggressively Fully remote, 4 weeks PTO, learning budget, co-working allowance, health & wellness support, and other benefits Access to top-tier AI tools (ChatGPT, Cursor, Hugging Face, Gemini, and more) Work alongside seasoned founders with a proven track record ⁉️ Other Questions Candidates Might Have 🛡️ On Safety & Ethics Some candidates will have questions about working in the adult AI space. Here's how to address it honestly: EverAI built EverGuard — a proprietary AI-powered moderation system designed to prevent prohibited content and ensure a safe environment for users The company is independently audited by a trusted external audit firm and overseen by a Board of Directors Payment providers, banks, and partners regularly audit EverAI to meet strict compliance standards The company has raised $10M from investors who conducted rigorous due diligence before investing This is not a grey-area operation. It is a compliance-first, investor-backed company that takes its responsibilities seriously. 🏆 Our Values These are the six values EverAI operates by: Aim Bigger, Go Faster Enjoy The Journey Make It Happen Stay Hungry, Stay Curious Own It, All of It Conquer Together 🎁 Our Benefits & Perks Flexible contract: regular employment or contractor, depending on location and preference Fully remote: work from anywhere in the world 4 weeks PTO (20 days annually) Health & wellness: $100/month allowance toward health insurance, plus unlimited 1:1 sessions with psychologists and lifestyle coaches via OpenUp (available to up to 3 family members too) Learning budget: for courses, books, conferences, or any resource that supports growth Co-working budget: up to 2 visits/month at €35/$40 per visit Company laptop & equipment: laptop provided, plus a monitor budget of up to $250 and a keyboard/mouse/mic/headphones budget of up to $150 Top-tier AI tools: ChatGPT, Gemini, Cursor, Hugging Face, and more Annual team gatherings: including CandyCon, our flagship company event Annual performance reviews: collaborative, two-way, tied to growth and career progression ⚠️ Reality Check: Who EverAI is NOT For Setting the right expectations upfront saves everyone time. Be direct with candidates about this before they go further in the process. EverAI is high-performance and fast-paced. We are NOT a fit for candidates who: Need fixed processes and clear playbooks to do their best work Take weeks to plan before executing — we move fast, sometimes shipping in hours Want a role with a narrow, defined scope and no expectation to go beyond it Only want to manage or oversee — everyone at EverAI is hands-on, always Struggle with accountability and ownership — we give a lot of trust, and we expect people to own their outcomes and raise their hand when something goes wrong ← Previous Do's and Don'ts Next → Preparing Candidates"},{"title":"Preparing Candidates — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"prepare-candidates.html","text":"How to Prepare Candidates for Interview(s) ℹ️ This page gives you everything you need to brief candidates before they enter our process. A well-prepared candidate performs better, drops out less, and reflects well on you and us, increasing our chances of success together. ☑️ How to Prepare Candidates Per Stage ℹ️ This applies to every candidate, at every level, for every role. Numbers and clarity are what separate the strong candidates in our process. We are a data-driven company, and we expect candidates to speak the same language. Interviewers will probe for specifics — candidates who rely on vague or general answers will not progress. Prepare every candidate to: Back everything with numbers: Growth percentages, budget sizes, timelines, user numbers, revenue impact. \"I improved conversion\" is not enough. \"I improved conversion from 1.2% to 2.8% over 3 months by testing X\" is what we expect. Show their specific individual impact: Not what the team did, but what they personally owned, decided, or built. Interviewers will ask \"what was your role specifically?\" for every example. Talk about achievements, not just responsibilities: What did they actually accomplish? What changed because of them ? What would not have happened if they hadn't been there? Prepare 2–3 strong success stories: With a clear situation, their specific action, and a measurable outcome. These should be ready to use across multiple stages. Be honest about failures too: We value self-awareness and humility. They should also have an example of something that didn't work, what they learned, and what they'd do differently. ➡️ Before the HM Screening Call Ask the candidate to: Read the Candidate Handbook Explore Candy.ai, as they should understand the product firsthand Be ready to speak clearly to why they want to work in this space specifically Prepare examples of ownership and impact: times they executed without being told what to do, made a decision under pressure, or built something from scratch ➡️ Before the Case Study / Technical Assessment Remind them that quality and structure matter more than speed Encourage them to ask clarifying questions upfront rather than making assumptions For technical roles: they should be prepared to justify decisions they make / made ➡️ Before the Cultural Fit Interview This is with a founder (typically CMO or CTO). Prepare candidates for: A direct, fast-paced conversation Questions about ownership, decision-making, and how they handle failure Being honest about what they don't know — humility is valued Sharing concrete examples, not hypotheticals ← Previous Pitching the Company Next → Hiring Internationally"},{"title":"Applicant Privacy Notice — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"privacy-notice.html","text":"EverAI Applicant Privacy Notice Last updated: 07 April 2026 1. Introduction EverAI Limited (\"EverAI\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal data you share with us during the recruitment and/or application process. EverAI is a \"controller\" in relation to such personal data. This means that we are responsible for deciding how we hold and use personal information about you. This EverAI Applicant Privacy Notice is intended to inform you about how and why your personal data will be used and stored during the recruitment and application process. 2. Data protection principles We will comply with data protection law and principles, which means that your data will be: Used lawfully, fairly and in a transparent way. Collected only for valid purposes that we have clearly explained and not used in any way that is incompatible with those purposes. Relevant to the purposes we have told you about and limited only to those purposes. Accurate and kept up to date. Kept only as long as necessary for the purposes we have told you about. Kept securely. 3. Who is your personal information collected from? We collect personal information about job candidates from the following sources: You, the applicant, when you apply for employment (e.g., directly through our website or through a job board) or respond to a proactive contact from us. Publicly accessible sources, e.g., professional profiles like LinkedIn or platforms that showcase your work or experience relevant to a role. Third parties with whom you have a pre-existing relationship and/or whom you authorize to provide us with information about you, including: referrers; recruitment agencies (for information on the data protection practices of recruitment agencies, please contact them directly); and your named references. 4. The kind of information we hold about you In connection with recruitment and/or your application for work with us, we will collect, store, and use the following categories of personal information about you: Information in our standard application form (name, email, contact information, link to LinkedIn profile, location, work authorization confirmation for your location (yes/no), timezone information, salary expectations, answers to other role-specific questions, portfolios or other documents needed to consider you for a particular role, and answers to any free fields in the application form). The information you have provided to us in your CV and/or additional documents that form part of your application. Any information you provide to us during your interview(s) or during the recruitment, interview, and hiring process. To facilitate hiring in our remote-first environment and accommodate varying timezones on the hiring team, we may ask to record interviews, so that all members of the hiring team can properly review the application. We will always ask for your consent before doing so, and it will always be clear in the call interface that a recording is in progress. We adhere to strict data deletion periods for any recordings (see Section 10 below). Automatically generated transcripts of any recorded interviews. Performance/results of any case study. We use this information solely to evaluate your fitness for the role. Information obtained from sources other than yourself previously referred to in this notice. Any legally mandated information per local requirements. You do not need to reveal, nor will we base our recruitment decisions on, any type of more sensitive information. However, if you voluntarily share this type of information (e.g., on your CV or in an interview), we may collect, store and process: Information about your race or ethnicity, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, sexual orientation and political opinions. Information about your gender identity and/or pronouns. Information about your health, including information necessary to accommodate any disability. Information about criminal convictions and offences. 5. How we will use information about you We will use the personal information we collect about you to: Assess your skills, qualifications, and suitability for the role. Carry out reference checks. Communicate with you and (as applicable) referring recruitment agencies about the recruitment process. Keep records related to our hiring processes. Comply with legal or regulatory requirements. Once we receive your application materials, we will process that information to decide whether you meet the basic requirements to be shortlisted for the role. If you do, we will decide whether your application is strong enough to invite you for an interview. If so, we will use the information you provide to us during your interview(s) to decide whether to make an offer of employment. If we decide to make such an offer, we will contact your references and/or perform any role-specific preliminary checks before making a final offer. You are responsible for informing your named references that you are giving us their contact information and obtaining any necessary consent for same. If you fail to provide requested information that is necessary for us to consider your application (such as evidence of qualifications or work history), we will not be able to process your application. As part of our recruitment process, we may use artificial intelligence (\"AI\") tools to assist in reviewing and summarizing application materials, parsing CV information, and transcribing interviews. These tools support human decision-making and are used to help organize and analyze information for the hiring team(s). AI systems used in this context do not materially influence employment decisions or make final hiring decisions, and candidates are never auto advanced or auto-rejected via AI tools. All recruitment- and application-relevant decisions are made by humans. 6. Legal bases for processing under European data protection law (e.g., GDPR, UK GDPR) To the extent required by applicable law, we process your personal information only according to the following legal bases: Legitimate interests : It is in our legitimate interests to determine applicants' fitness for a particular role, and to ultimately make hiring decisions, so as to appropriately staff the company; to engage appropriate third parties (e.g., a centralized recruitment management platform) to assist in same; and to record interviews and store them for a limited period of time, to facilitate hiring in a remote-first environment and accommodate varying timezones on the hiring team. Contractual necessity : We need to process your personal information to decide whether to enter into a contract (of employment) with you. Legal obligation : Where a relevant legal obligation applies (e.g., confirming your right to work from your location), our processing is based on the same. Consent : In limited circumstances, we may base processing activities on your informed consent, for example, when processing information that you voluntarily offer and (in the event we do not move forward with your application) retaining your application materials for future roles. Where we rely on consent as our legal basis for processing your data, you may withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the future. If we process any special category data provided as part of your application (e.g., health, religious, or ethnicity information), this is based on Art. 9(2)(b) of the GDPR, which relates to our obligations in employment. Depending on the circumstances, we may rely on different legal bases when processing the same information for different purposes. If you reside outside the EEA, UK, or Switzerland, the legal bases on which we rely may differ from those listed above. 7. Automated decision-making You will not be subject to decisions that will have a significant impact on you based solely on automated decision-making. While EverAI may use AI tools for purposes consistent with this Applicant Privacy Notice, these tools operate only as decision-support systems and do not materially influence or independently determine application- or hiring-relevant decisions. 8. Disclosure of your personal information We will only share your personal information with third parties where necessary for us to process your application. The parties to whom we may disclose your personal information include: EverAI staff on the applicable hiring team : Internal staff receive information about your application on a need-to-know basis and are subject to confidentiality obligations. Generally, only members of the hiring team for a given role and top-level management have access to your application information. Service providers : We use service providers to facilitate our hiring processes, including office tools and a centralized recruitment management platform. These service providers may only use your information to perform certain tasks on our behalf and have access only to the information needed to perform such tasks that we define. All third-party service providers or other recipients are required to take appropriate security measures to protect your personal information in line with applicable law. Recruitment agencies : If your application came in through a recruitment agency, we share limited information regarding the status of your application with them upon request. Other third parties required by law : We take our legal obligations seriously, and may access, preserve, and share personal information with regulators, public authorities, law enforcement, government agencies, or others, where we reasonably believe such disclosure is necessary to comply with valid legal process, court orders, applicable law, regulations, or official requests; address illegal or suspected illegal activities, security, or technical issues; protect against harm to the rights, property or safety of our company, users, staff, or other third parties; or maintain and protect the security and integrity of our infrastructure. Your personal information may also be transferred outside the EEA or UK in connection with the application and recruitment process. As a remote-first environment, our staff (and members of the hiring team and management) are located and may access your information from outside the EEA or UK. Some of our service providers, including our centralized recruitment platform (Ashby), are also located outside the EEA or UK, including in the United States of America. When we transfer personal information outside the EEA or UK, we ensure that the transfer complies with this privacy notice and applicable law. Where an appropriate safeguard for transfers of personal information outside the EEA or UK is required, we generally rely on adequacy decisions published by, and/or Standard Contractual Clauses approved by, the European Commission and/or UK Information Commissioner's Office. 9. Data security We have put in place appropriate security measures to prevent your personal information from being accidentally lost, used or accessed in an unauthorized way, altered or disclosed. In addition, we limit access to your personal information to those employees, agents, contractors and other third parties who have a need to know. They will only process your personal information on our instructions and they are subject to a duty of confidentiality. We have put in place procedures to deal with any suspected data security breach and will notify you and any applicable regulator of a suspected breach where we are legally required to do so. 10. Data retention General retention period : We will retain your personal information for the duration of your application/recruitment process, and for two years after communicating the outcome of your application. We retain your personal information for that period so that: if you apply for another role, we have a record of previous decisions taken on your application; with your consent, we can consider you for future roles for which you may be a good fit; and, for applications coming through a recruitment agency, to fulfill our obligations under our contracts with them (e.g., when we are required to pay a commission for rejected applicants who are later hired within a specified period after the initial referral). Specific retention periods: Any recorded interviews are deleted 4 months after recording. Information relating to successful applicants will be transferred to their employment records, insofar as the information is necessary to establish an employment relationship or comply with legal obligations. In this case, retention periods are subject to our separate EverAI Staff Privacy Notice. 11. Your rights related to your personal information Depending on your location, applicable legal requirements, and applicable exemptions, you have certain rights with respect to your personal information: Right of access : You have the right to request access to your personal information, namely, receive a copy of the personal information we hold about you and to check that we are lawfully processing it. Right to rectification : You have the right to request rectification of the personal information that we hold about you, namely, have any incomplete or inaccurate information we hold about you corrected. Right to deletion : You have the right to request deletion of your personal information. Right to object : In some cases, you have the right to object to us processing your personal information where we are relying on our or a third party's legitimate interest. Right to restrict processing : In some cases, you have the right to request restriction of processing of your personal information. Right to file a complaint : If you are in the EEA or the UK, you also have a right to file a complaint with your local data protection authority. You can exercise the above rights by contacting us at hello@everai.ai . We will respond to any data-related request as soon as practicable, and in any event within 30 days of receipt. We may require further information from you to verify the request, i.e., to ensure that it is really you making the request, or that any third-party requester has authority to act on your behalf. 12. California Applicants In addition to the rights explained in this Applicant Privacy Notice, California residents also have rights under The California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018 (\"CCPA\"), as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act, subject to the exceptions therein. Applicants residing in California additionally have the right to: Certain information concerning our collection and use of their personal information; Request that we delete certain personal information we collected from them; Appoint an agent to exercise their rights provided for by the CCPA, provided that we are able to verify the request from a third-party via a duly executed notarized power of attorney and sufficient information to allow us to verify your identity and locate your information in our systems; Not be subjected to discrimination for the exercise of these rights. We do not sell (and have not sold in the past 12 months) your personal information to third parties. We do not share (and have not shared in the past 12 months) your personal information with third parties for cross-context behavioral advertising purposes. 13. Additional inquiries If you have any additional questions not addressed in this Applicant Privacy Notice, please contact us at hello@everai.ai . ← Previous Get in Touch"},{"title":"Senior Product Designer — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"product-designer.html","text":"Department R&D Hiring Manager Arni Lochner (Design Lead) Location Europe Contract B2B / contractor to start, potential transition to full-time Openings 2 Seniorities Senior Budget €80,000–€100,000 (total package) — target range. Up to €120,000 only for genuinely exceptional candidates; this is not the standard offer. Ask for compensation expectations and alignment with this range — never current or previous salary. 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, location default, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role, including two explicit exceptions to that page's defaults: the B2B/contractor engagement model and the mandatory AI-usage gate. ⛔️ Top Requirements AI-native design workflow — hard requirement, not a nice-to-have. Strong senior-level product design craft. Strong product judgment / taste. Strategic product thinking, not UI execution alone. Ability to ideate and contribute to product direction. Strong communication, reasoning, and ability to challenge/push back constructively. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For EverAI / Candy.ai — see 🗣️ Pitching the Company for the full story and scale. Hands-on, end-to-end design across chat experiences, character creation, monetisation and growth flows, and emerging surfaces (live/interactive features, AI video). Works directly with the Design Lead (Arni), PMs, and founders — high autonomy, often the only designer on a surface. Mobile-first. We are not looking for someone who primarily receives requirements and turns them into polished screens. We want a senior designer who understands the product/user problem, generates and challenges ideas, makes and explains strong product/design decisions, and moves from ambiguity toward a strong solution — using AI actively in that workflow. A separate, candidate-facing JD exists for external sharing — ask your TA contact for it. ⛔️ Screening Criteria AI-native workflow — one of only four roles company-wide with an explicit mandatory AI-usage gate (alongside Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer, Senior Product Manager, and AI Cinematic Video Editor/Creator). Uses AI tools daily for design, prototyping, or content generation (Claude, Cursor, image/video gen, code-based prototyping) — real prompting, experimentation, and AI-assisted creation, not just familiarity. Can talk specifics, not aspirations. Product design craft — end-to-end consumer product design, mobile-first, shipped at real scale (approximately 5+ years). Can explain the problem, constraints, options considered, decisions made, trade-offs, and final outcome — not just show polished screens. Advanced Figma and strong prototyping (design-tool and/or code-based). Product judgment / taste — distinguishes a strong product experience from merely polished UI: clear reasoning, prioritization, thoughtful trade-offs, ability to simplify. Not reducible to subjective visual preference. Strategic / product thinking — contributes to what should be built and why, not only how it should look. Ideation — generates ideas and alternative solutions rather than waiting for fully formed requirements. Communication / pushback — defends decisions, challenges weak assumptions, disagrees constructively, explains reasoning clearly, and changes their mind when evidence is stronger. Async communication quality (concise writing, brief-following) is a strong predictor for this fully remote team. Ownership — can distinguish what they personally did from what the team did. 🎨 Portfolio evidence: a visually polished portfolio alone is not sufficient. Strong case studies show problem/context, the candidate's personal role, reasoning, alternatives/trade-offs, product thinking, decisions, outcome, and what changed because of their work. Also confirms comfort with NSFW/adult product experiences (asked directly, early) and the B2B/contractor-to-full-time engagement model (confirmed explicitly on the first call, logged in writing) — see the shared Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags guide for the general framework. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Primarily UI/visual execution with weak product thinking. Portfolio shows final screens but little reasoning; vague ownership — unclear what they did vs. their team. Waits for PMs to define the solution before designing; weak ideation. Cannot explain trade-offs, or cannot challenge/push back constructively. No meaningful current AI usage, or talks about AI conceptually without demonstrating how it changes their actual workflow. Highly polished presentation masking weak ownership or product judgment. Portfolio red flags: text-heavy/visual-light, messy typography, overly academic UX process (sticky-note walls, double-diamond diagrams, endless wireframe journeys before any design), not mobile-optimised, outdated device mockups, wrong work mix (branding/logos, marketing pages, Web3, dashboards, templated SaaS, corporate B2B), over-animated theatrics, dated hosting (WordPress/Squarespace/Canva), spelling mistakes or broken links. Do not reject candidates merely for coming from an agency, consultancy, startup, smaller company, or an unconventional background — assess craft and evidence on their own merits. Be cautious with freelancers or studio owners with little in-house experience (probe commitment and ability to operate inside a team) but don't rule them out. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What's your current situation, and why are you exploring? (Listen for counter-offer dynamics.) Why EverAI? Did you review Candy.ai and the Handbook? What draws you to AI companionship as a space? Which product areas did you fully own, concept → launch, in your last role? Walk me through the single screen or flow you're proudest of — why does it work? (Craft probe.) Tell me about a time you proposed or significantly changed a product direction, rather than just executing a spec you were given. (Ideation probe.) Tell me about a time you disagreed with a PM, founder, or stakeholder on a design decision — how did you make your case, and what happened? (Pushback probe.) How do AI tools sit in your day-to-day design workflow — which ones, for what, concretely? Give a recent example. How do you evaluate or correct the output? Have you designed for sensitive/NSFW categories? What was your hands-on involvement? You'd be engaged B2B/contractor initially, with potential transition to full-time — does that work for you? (Record answer verbatim; also confirm country of residence — tax/contract setup varies, don't assume from nationality.) Location / compensation expectations / notice period? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: NSFW/dating/AI-companionship domain experience Motion, 3D, illustration Subscription/monetisation products Gamification Front-end fluency (HTML/CSS/JS) ✅ Positive portfolio signals: custom domain built on Framer or Webflow; animation & interaction shown in case studies; strong, concise visual and written communication; clean/modern/premium aesthetic; at least one strong relevant case study plus a second meaningfully related one (B2C, AI-driven, social/entertainment); demonstrated impact (outcomes, results, or clear rationale). 🏷️ Titles candidates may hold: Senior Product Designer, Lead Product Designer, Senior UI/UX Designer, Senior Interaction Designer, Product Design Lead (smaller companies), UX/UI Lead, Product Designer II, Digital/Creative Designer. Calibration — Example Profiles That Fit Use these as the taste benchmark: if a submitted profile wouldn't sit comfortably next to these, it's a pass. Anton Blinkov — Apple Design Award (Loona); multiple shipped consumer apps; motion/interaction-savvy; clear problem→solution→results case studies. Kristina Lenberg — motion-led storytelling; shipped at Snapchat and Tabby; outcome-focused case studies; strong systems thinking with visual innovation. Arni Lochner — example candidate for calibration. 📁 Sourcing Guidance Industry Target companies 💘 Dating, relationship & social platforms — sensitive verticals, retention + monetisation UX Feeld, Grindr, Tinder, Hily, HUD, Bumble, Telegram 🤖 AI companionship apps — closest to our category Eva AI, Lovescape, Our Dream, JOI, Replika 🎬 Content-generation tools — adjacent signal Higgsfield, Leonardo AI, Krea, Runway 📱 Subscription consumer apps — onboarding, conversion, retention Headspace, Blinkist, Duolingo, Calm 🎮 Live-interactive / gamified products — engagement mechanics IMVU, Tango, StripChat. Design quality at these companies is generally weak — domain experience here only counts if paired with a strong, modern portfolio. ℹ️ Sourcing aid only, not a qualification or rejection rule — a strong candidate from outside these companies is still in play; assess craft and evidence on their own merits. 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. The case study is a scoped design exercise (~4–5 hrs, clear written brief, includes a ≤5-minute Loom walkthrough with working audio); the final round is with founders (Thomas, Mike). 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager (Arni) — 30 min → 3 Case Study — ~4–5 hrs → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer Set the full process in writing up front — no fast-tracks or skipped steps, regardless of seniority, referral, or counter-offer pressure; a candidate repeatedly probing to shorten it is a culture-fit flag. Referrers stay fully outside the process (no task selection, feedback, or candidate communication) — route candidate questions to Arni or your TA contact only. ← Previous AI Cinematic Video Editor Next → Security Engineer"},{"title":"Our Recruitment Process — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"recruitment-process.html","text":"What You Can Expect We respect your time and energy. Our recruitment process is designed to be rigorous yet efficient, ensuring we find the best A-players while giving you a transparent look into how we work. While the specific steps may vary slightly depending on the role, here is the general roadmap of your journey with EverAI : 📄 Step 1: Application Review After your application, a member of our team will review your application personally. We look for impact, speed, and alignment with our values. 🤝 Step 2: Culture & Discovery Call Who: A member of our Talent Acquisition team. Goal: To get to know you! We'll discuss your background, your interest in EverAI, and answer your initial questions about the company. We want to ensure our culture of speed and ownership is a match for what you are looking for. 🧠 Step 3: Hiring Manager(s) Deep Dive Who: Your potential future manager or a colleague from the team. Goal: A deeper conversation about your expertise. We'll dig into your past projects, the challenges you've solved, and the \"wins\" you are most proud of. This is your chance to geek out on your craft. 💻 Step 4: The Challenge / Case Study What: A practical assessment or take-home task. Goal: We believe in \"Show, Don't Tell.\" Whether it's a coding challenge, a design task, or a strategic case study, this step allows you to showcase your skills in a real-world context similar to the work you'd do here. 🚀 Step 5: Founder Round / Cultural Fit Interview Who: Key stakeholders, cross-functional peers, or our Co-Founders. Goal: The final sanity check. We assess \"Culture Add\": how you will raise the bar for the team, and alignment on our long-term vision. 🎉 Step 6: Reference Check & Offer Goal: We speak to your former peers/managers to understand how to set you up for success (don't worry, we will never contact anyone without your permission). Then, if it's a match, we roll out the red carpet with an offer to join the rocket ship! 📹 A Note on AI Interview Recordings To support a consistent and fair hiring process in our remote-first environment, we use AI note-taking tools during interviews so interviewers can focus on the conversation rather than manual note-taking. Consent is requested where required, and recording is always visible during the interview. Rest assured, these recordings are strictly confidential , used solely for hiring decisions, and are permanently deleted after 4 months , in accordance with our Applicant Privacy Notice . How to Ace the Interview Most candidates don't fail interviews because they lack intelligence or relevant experience; they fail because they lack precision . In a high-velocity environment, we don't just value talent; we value reliability . The candidates who perform best communicate clearly, focus on outcomes, and remove unnecessary detail. Here is how to stand out in your interview process: 🎯 Prioritize Precision over Explanation Don't just tell us what you did; tell us why it mattered . When using the STAR Method , keep the \"Situation\" brief and spend 80% of your time on Actions and Results . Stay Objective: Focus on outcomes, not emotions. Quantify Everything: Did you increase retention by 15%? Did you cut latency by 200ms? Numbers are the language of trust. ⚡ Show Your Velocity One of our core values is \"Aim Bigger, Go Faster.\" We look for a bias toward action. Share examples of when you chose \"done\" over \"perfect\" or iterated on a project in record time. Show us you can handle the speed of a remote, high-growth team. 📢 Be Concise & Direct In a remote, high-speed environment, clear communication is a superpower. Be Concise: If your answer feels long, it is. Keep it sharp. Kill the Acronyms: Speak plainly. Clarity is more impressive than sounding technical. The \"I Don't Know\" Rule: If you're stuck, don't ramble. Say: \"I don't know the answer to that yet, but here is exactly how I would find out.\" 🕵️ Ask Genuine & High-Signal Questions Skip the generic, ChatGPT-generated questions. We want to see real curiosity about Candy.ai . Ask us about our roadmap, our specific technical debt, or the biggest bottleneck we're facing this quarter. Show us you've already started thinking like an employee. ✨ Be Authentic & Grounded We hire people, not resumes. You don't need to be a \"perfect\" candidate; you need to be a precise one. Bring your unique perspective, your real challenges, and your honest experiences; failures included. 😮‍💨 Take a Breath, You've Got This! If you encounter a tricky question, take a moment to gather your thoughts. Thoughtfulness and confidence always leave a good impression. ← Previous Why Join Us? Next → Get in Touch"},{"title":"Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"red-flags.html","text":"Quick Decision Guide Scan this first. Full detail and probes are below. ⛔ Stop / Do Not Progress Clear hard-gate failures. NSFW / explicit-content refusal where the role requires exposure Contract / working-model incompatibility Location / timezone incompatibility with the role's requirement Compensation materially outside approved range, no flexibility Conflicting full-time employment where the role requires full-time commitment English insufficient to perform the role's actual responsibilities 🔍 Explore / Verify Needs evidence or clarification before you decide. Cannot separate personal ownership from team results Claims scale or seniority without evidence Cannot show measurable impact Hands-on capability is stale or delegated Adjacent experience presented as direct experience Answers too unclear to assess competence Excessive negativity/blame, or repeated short tenures without a coherent explanation ✅ Positive Signal Strengthens a candidate — not automatically required. Strong career progression / increasing scope Specific, credible examples with measurable outcomes Clear personal-vs-team distinction Practical AI usage with good judgment Operating independently; building tools/workflows Admits mistakes and explains what changed after ⛔ Admin / Eligibility Objective requirements. Check these early. Requirement Hard stop when Confirm NSFW / explicit content Not comfortable working for an adult / explicit-content product, or unwilling to handle explicit content where the role requires direct exposure. Comfort working in an explicit-content environment (script below). B2B / working model Refuses the required contractor setup, or cannot practically work under it. B2B acceptance, country of residence. Location / timezone Cannot meet the role's location requirement or working overlap, or needs relocation/visa support the role doesn't provide. Against the role brief's exact requirement. Compensation Expectations materially outside the approved range, and not flexible. Expectations against the published range. Availability / commitment Timing genuinely doesn't work, or candidate intends to retain another full-time job where full-time is required. Notice period, earliest start date, competing commitments. English Insufficient to perform the actual responsibilities of the role. Ability to work and communicate in the role's required language, in context. 💬 NSFW confirmation script: \"Our products can include explicit / NSFW content. Are you fully comfortable working in this environment as part of your day-to-day role?\" 🌍 Location default: Europe, or a nearby timezone with strong overlap with European working hours, unless the individual role brief explicitly says otherwise. The role-specific rule always wins over this default. Notes Previous adult-industry experience is not required unless the role brief says otherwise. Use the role brief for the exact location/timezone requirement. Asking about compensation is not a red flag — ask for expectations and range alignment, never current or previous salary. A long notice period or side project is not automatically a rejection. 🚩 Hard Skills / Evidence These are evidence problems. The role brief defines the exact technical or functional bar. 1. Ownership is unclear Relies on \"we\", \"the team\", or company-level outcomes; can't isolate their own contribution. Probe: What was specifically yours? Which decisions did you personally make? What did someone else own? 2. Scale is presented without personal control Large company, team, or project numbers are presented as personal achievements without evidence of direct control or contribution. Probe: What part was directly under your control? What did you personally change? What measurable outcome followed? 3. No concrete, measurable impact Describes responsibilities but can't explain outcomes, even when repeatedly asked — e.g. revenue, growth, conversion, retention, quality, reliability, delivery speed, product usage, risk reduction, operational efficiency, cost reduction, or other role-relevant KPIs. A senior candidate who repeatedly avoids measurable outcomes is a stronger version of this same gap. 4. Claims don't reconcile, or numbers don't add up Facts shift across CV, application, and interview, or figures don't make sense when examined (timelines, team size, budget, scope). Probe: Walk me through this timeline again. How does that number break down? 5. \"NDA\" used as a blanket excuse Confidentiality is real, but it shouldn't prevent describing their own role, decisions, and approach in general terms. Probe: Without naming the client/product, what did you personally decide, build, or change? 6. Hands-on capability is no longer current Now mainly manages, coordinates, advises, or delegates work that the role requires them to execute personally. Probe: What did you personally execute recently? Which relevant tools/workflows/processes do you still use yourself? When did you last do this work hands-on? Seniority itself is not a red flag. 7. Adjacent experience is presented as direct experience Examples: management presented as execution, strategy presented as delivery, reporting presented as analysis ownership, advisory work presented as operational ownership, coordination presented as functional expertise. The role brief defines what counts as relevant experience. 8. Overlapping or stacked roles Multiple concurrent roles/employers on the timeline without a clear explanation of how each was handled. Probe: How did you manage both at once? What did each one actually involve? 🎯 Company name, title, or pedigree are sourcing signals — not proof of fit. Always validate ownership, depth, recency, scale, results, and decision-making. Use evidence and context — don't automatically reject on any single item above. ⚠️ Cultural Fit / Soft Skills Signals to explore. Do not reject on these alone without evidence. Poor preparation / low engagement Did they review the company/role? Can they explain why they're interested? Do they show useful curiosity? Do not judge based on visible energy or extroversion. Low ownership in ambiguity Can they move forward without a complete playbook? Can they make reasonable decisions independently? Can they ask for clarity without becoming blocked? Cannot discuss mistakes constructively Can they identify something that failed? Can they explain what they learned or would change? Do they get defensive when challenged? Persistent blame / disrespect Immediate concern when clearly demonstrated Discriminatory/degrading comments, disrespect toward recruiters/interviewers, hostility or repeated dismissiveness. Explore when Every previous employer/manager is blamed; candidate takes no ownership in conflicts; cannot discuss difficult experiences constructively. Repeated short tenures A question, not a rejection criterion. Check: layoffs, contracts, acquisitions, restructuring, project-based work, role mismatch, other reasonable explanations. Ask: what led to each move? Communication prevents assessment Can you understand what they did, what they owned, why they made decisions, and what happened? Do they repeatedly avoid answering the actual question asked? Perfect English, charisma, or presentation style are not the standard unless the role explicitly requires them. 🤖 AI usage is generally a positive signal, not a company-wide hard gate. Only treat it as mandatory when the individual role brief explicitly says so. ✅ Positive Signals Useful evidence that strengthens a candidate — not automatically required. Strong career progression / increasing scope Specific and credible examples Clear personal-vs-team distinction Recent achievements with measurable outcomes Strong ownership Explains decisions and trade-offs Learns quickly Good product/company preparation Strong questions Practical AI usage with good judgment Builds tools/workflows to solve problems Evidence of operating independently Admits mistakes and explains what changed after None of these are hard requirements — they're what makes an eligible, evidence-backed candidate stand out. ✅ Not a Red Flag by Itself Asking about compensation or benefits Asking about workload / working hours Asking detailed process questions Being laid off Career break Contract / freelance experience Consulting background Short tenures with reasonable explanation No previous adult/NSFW industry experience unless the role requires it No AI background unless the role requires it Introverted / lower-energy communication style Respectfully challenging assumptions Asking for clarity Coming from outside target-company lists Non-traditional career path Different job title with equivalent responsibilities No promotion / lack of career progression Assess evidence against the role brief, not proxies. Before You Submit Eligibility: Are all admin hard gates cleared? Role fit: Do they meet the role-specific hard-skill bar? Ownership: What did they personally own? Evidence: What concrete evidence supports the submission? Concerns: Is any meaningful concern still unresolved? ⚠️ If you cannot answer these five questions, do not submit the candidate yet. Individual role briefs override this page for technical requirements, level, compensation, location, mandatory domain experience, and role-specific hard gates. ← Previous How to Use Ashby Next → Our Open Roles"},{"title":"Helpful Resources — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"resources.html","text":"Candidate Handbook ↗ Job Board ↗ Website ↗ LinkedIn Page ↗ Glassdoor Page ↗ 🚧 This document is a WIP, and our TA team is working on building more resources for you. If you don't see what you're looking for, please feel free to reach out to your recruiter anytime. We're partners, and we're here to answer any questions you may have along the way! 🤝 ← Previous Off-Limits Companies"},{"title":"Role Briefs","url":"roles.html","text":"Active roles 📈 Performance Marketer ↗ 👩‍💻 Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer ↗ 🎥 AI Cinematic Video Editor ↗ 🎨 Product Designer ↗ 🔒 Security Engineer ↗ 🤝 Senior Affiliate Manager ↗ 📬 Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager ↗ 🧭 Senior Product Manager ↗ 🛡️ Content Moderator ↗ 📊 Business Analyst ↗ Not currently open 🗄️ Past Briefs ↗"},{"title":"Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"ruby-engineer.html","text":"Department R&D Hiring Manager Juan Miguel Location Europe Timezone CET ±3 Budget Target ~€100K · up to €120K for exceptional candidates only Openings 2 Seniorities Senior 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (NSFW, B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role, including one explicit exception to that page's defaults. ⛔️ Top Requirements Recent hands-on production Ruby on Rails experience. Senior backend engineering depth / technical reasoning. Based in Europe, with CET ±3 working-hours overlap. Active AI-development-tool usage, with ability to inspect/correct/explain generated code. Strong personal technical ownership. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For Primary backend stack is Ruby on Rails. Production-scale/high-traffic experience is relevant — engineering decisions here have immediate product consequences. Engineers are hands-on and work cross-functionally, with PMs, Designers, QA, and AI/DevOps. ⛔️ Screening Criteria What matters is what the candidate actually built and owned in production Ruby on Rails — not the size or fame of the company they built it at. Agency, consulting, freelance, startup, and smaller product-company backgrounds are all valid; none of them are weaker by default than a big-name employer. Senior depth is judged by ownership and execution, not years of experience alone. Recent, hands-on production Ruby on Rails work — their daily reality, not a side project or occasional task. Personal technical ownership — built and owned, works independently and quickly. Senior technical reasoning — explains trade-offs clearly. Independent debugging / verification discipline. Active AI-tool usage — currently uses AI development tools (e.g. Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code, ChatGPT) and can inspect, correct, and explain AI-generated code, not just accept it. ⚠️ AI tool usage is a hard requirement, not a nice-to-have. This is one of only 4 roles company-wide (with Product Designer, Senior Product Manager, and AI Cinematic Video Editor/Creator) where active AI usage in the day-to-day workflow is a genuine hard gate rather than a positive signal. No AI usage at all is an immediate no. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Ruby experience is stale or side-project only. Cannot explain personal technical decisions or trade-offs. Cannot reason through debugging or verification independently. No AI-tool usage in their workflow. Accepts AI-generated code without verification or correction. Overly managerial / distant from hands-on execution. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. Can you briefly walk me through your current role and main responsibilities? What is the biggest technical challenge you faced in the last 6 months? What options did you weigh, and why did you choose the approach you did? Why are you considering a move now? (If applicable) You've had some leadership exposure — why are you interested in a Senior IC position rather than continuing in management? Tell me about a time you had to debug or verify something quickly, working independently. Have you tried Candy.ai ? What do you think about it? Our flagship product involves AI companionship and adult-oriented content. Are you fully comfortable working in an environment that can include NSFW or adult themes, handled respectfully and professionally? Do you use AI tools in your development workflow? Which ones, and how do you verify or correct what they produce before it ships? What are the top 2–3 things you're looking for in your next opportunity? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: Experience with monolithic architecture and/or scaling challenges strong positive signal Comfortable in a startup environment : ambiguity, fast iteration, direct communication strong positive signal High-traffic B2C/SaaS exposure, broad product responsibility, scale-up experience, or strong career progression positive signal, not required Healthcare, government, and similarly regulated or slow-moving backgrounds have historically been a weaker match for our pace — evaluate on the same ownership/depth bar above rather than rejecting by industry alone. 📁 Sourcing Guidance ⚠️ No approved target-company list yet. Source based on the profile above (high-traffic Ruby on Rails shops — B2C or SaaS products running Rails at real production scale). Confirm with Juan Miguel before treating any specific company list as validated. Target companies are a sourcing aid, not a qualification or rejection rule — a candidate from an agency, a consultancy, a startup, or an unlisted smaller product company is assessed on the same bar: what they personally built, owned, and can explain. 🔄 Interview Process Role-specific exception to the shared default (see ⏳ Hiring Process ): the case study is replaced with a live coding exercise. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Live Coding — 2 hrs, live → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Performance Marketer Next → AI Cinematic Video Editor"},{"title":"Safety and Ethics — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"safety-and-ethics.html","text":"Overview 🚀 Safety and ethics are at the core of our product and mission. We recognize our unique responsibility as an adults-only AI platform, and we take a safety-by-design approach, embedding safety into all aspects of our operation and all stages of the development lifecycle. We know that you're reading this because safety is important to you, too. This document aims to strike a balance between providing meaningful information on our moderation controls while not compromising security by giving bad actors information on how to evade them. If you have specific questions about safety that aren't addressed here, we're happy to answer them during your interviews. Technical and organizational measures Technical measures Users cannot upload or import external visual media to the platform. This prevents, for example, non-consensual intimate imagery and \"nudification.\" All text and images are subject to moderation. We incorporate layered safeguards on the platform, continuous monitoring, and dedicated oversight to maintain safety and integrity. Through ongoing collaboration between our Trust & Safety and AI teams, we are constantly improving and refining our proprietary moderation LLM (EverGuard), the top adult moderation tool worldwide. Because our moderation technology is proprietary and security-sensitive, we can't share detailed implementation or infrastructure information publicly. You are invited to ask more specific questions during any interviews, and your interviewers will be happy to share more detailed information. Organizational measures Ensuring safety and ethics in our products is not a one-and-done or \"check the box\" exercise. It requires a culture of compliance, buy-in from top-level management, and an organizational commitment to safety. The following gives an overview of how we've built a culture of compliance at EverAI: We have a zero-tolerance policy for Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM) and are committed to fully complying with valid requests from law enforcement. In addition to our other content moderation and removal controls, human moderators review flagged accounts and permanently block users that attempt to create CSAM. We are a registered reporter with and report known CSAM to the National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (or other local authorities as appropriate). We have an in-house Ethics and Compliance Officer (ECO) who owns safety and compliance issues. This is not simply a title given to someone in the company; the position was specifically recruited-for. Our ECO works with all teams on an ongoing basis to address compliance and/or safety topics that come up in their work, for example, reviewing new features and characters before they are published on the platform. All EverAI team members' onboarding includes safety/compliance trainings. Additional company-wide and department-specific trainings on safety and broader compliance topics (e.g., data protection) are also provided on an ongoing basis. ℹ️ You can access our Trust & Safety hub . ← Previous What We Do Next → Engineering at EverAI"},{"title":"Security Engineer — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"security-engineer.html","text":"Department R&D Hiring Leads Robin Razzi + Michael Monin Location Europe (CET overlap required, 80%) Openings 1 Seniorities Mid or Senior Budget Mid: €65K–€85K. Senior: €85K–€115K. Top of each band is reserved for exceptional candidates, not the standard offer — align on compensation expectations against the range during screening. 🔗 See 🚩 Candidate Hard Gates & Red Flags for company-wide eligibility rules (B2B, location default, English, compensation-expectations screening). What follows is specific to this role, including the daily-exposure NSFW note below. 🔞 Daily work involves NSFW exposure on Candy.ai . Do not submit candidates unless NSFW comfort has been explicitly confirmed on a call. ⛔️ Top Requirements Practical, hands-on security ownership — not a compliance-only seat. Git/GitHub fluency — comfortable shipping code and working within engineering workflows, not just reviewing from the outside. Scripting/automation skills — Python/Bash or equivalent. Prior experience at another AI company or a scale-up (50+ employees). CET timezone overlap (~80%) — required for daily collaboration. Comfortable with occasional nights & weekend security monitoring/on-call coverage. 🎯 What We Are Hiring For A hands-on Security Engineer to own application security, GRC, and security awareness — not a compliance-only seat. You'll code-review, drive vulnerability remediation, build out the risk register, coordinate external audits/pentests, and carry occasional weekend monitoring coverage, with real ownership from day one. Reports directly to Robin Razzi (QA Lead), who brings hands-on security experience and can go deep on technical topics; Michael Monin (CTO & Co-founder) is also a stakeholder on this hire. The candidate will be the sole dedicated security hire — comfortable owning the function independently day-to-day. Broad security generalist seat spanning Application Security, GRC, Security Awareness, IT/Access Management (MDM, provisioning), and emerging AI-specific threats — not a single-specialty role. ⛔️ Screening Criteria Practical ownership — can distinguish \"I identified / implemented / fixed / improved\" from \"the security team was responsible for.\" The hands-on, code-reviewing, remediation-driving profile above is what's being tested, not theoretical knowledge. Application Security — practical involvement identifying, prioritizing, and resolving security issues, not just familiarity with concepts. GRC / security governance — experience building or maintaining a risk register and coordinating external audits/pentests, proportionate to this being one part of a broader generalist scope, not the whole role. Risk judgment — can identify meaningful risks, prioritize them, explain trade-offs, and determine proportionate remediation. Company-stage fit — 2–3+ years hands-on security experience (application security, GRC, or a mix); flexible on years given AI-startup intensity (e.g. ~1 year at Candy can weigh like ~3 years elsewhere). \"Hacker\" mindset — independently experiments, breaks things, researches vulnerabilities, and builds original security projects outside of formal processes. 🤖 AI usage is a positive signal for this role, not a hard requirement. Awareness of emerging AI-specific threats is part of the broader scope; hands-on use of AI tools (code review, vulnerability research, workflow automation) is useful evidence of the \"hacker\" mindset above, but its absence is not disqualifying — unlike Ruby Engineer, Product Designer, or Senior Product Manager, where it is mandatory. Also confirms NSFW comfort (explicitly, before submission — see the callout above) and CET overlap / weekend on-call comfort. Security Awareness and IT/Access Management (MDM, provisioning) are part of the role's broader scope; probe them lightly rather than as separate deep-dive gates. 🚩 Red Flags 🚩 Security experience is almost entirely theoretical. Purely audit/compliance profile with insufficient practical/hands-on security work. Cannot explain personal ownership — relies on \"we\"/\"the security team\" rather than personal contribution. Cannot give concrete examples of security issues personally identified/resolved. Cannot prioritize risk or explain trade-offs. Overly process-heavy approach with no evidence of implementation. No Git/engineering fluency — cannot operate inside engineering workflows. Not comfortable with weekend/on-call coverage or the required CET overlap. NSFW comfort is hesitant. Do not reject candidates merely for coming from consulting, a smaller company, or a particular security specialty — assess practical ownership and evidence on their own merits. 💬 Recruiter Screening Questions ℹ️ Use these questions during your screening call. Include a summary of the candidate's answers in your submission notes in Ashby. What are your main responsibilities in your current security role, and why are you considering a move? Have you seen Candy.ai ? Our product operates in the AI companionship space and generates adult/NSFW content — are you fully comfortable working with this content on a daily basis? Walk me through a security risk or vulnerability you personally identified and resolved (explain it to me as if I'm not technical). What did you personally do, versus what the wider team handled? Have you worked with external security auditors or penetration-testing firms before? What tools or platforms have you used for vulnerability management, code review, or GRC/risk tracking? If you joined a company with no risk register or documented risks, how would you start? (Note the answer for technical review, no need to judge quality yourself.) Tell me about a time you had to balance a security risk against a product or business constraint — how did you decide, and what happened? How do you think about securing AI-enabled products, or have you encountered AI-specific security risks? Do you use AI tools yourself (for code review, vulnerability research, or workflow automation)? Are you comfortable with a role that includes occasional nights & weekend monitoring/on-call coverage? Location / compensation expectations / notice period / B2B? What questions do you have for me? 🎯 Strong Signals / Sourcing Guidance Positive signals — not automatic hard gates: Application/product security engineers from AI startups that scaled up (ideally 100–500 person scale-ups). Comfortable being the sole or most senior security voice. Hands-on use of AI tools (code review, vulnerability research, workflow automation) — evidence of the \"hacker\" mindset, not required. Broad security ownership across AppSec/GRC/awareness/access rather than a single specialty. ⚠️ No approved target-company list yet. Source based on the profile above (AI startups at scale-up stage where the candidate was the sole/most senior security voice, or hands-on AppSec/GRC experience at a security tooling vendor). Confirm with Robin before treating any specific company list as validated. Target companies are a sourcing aid only — a candidate from an unlisted company is assessed on the same bar. 🔄 Interview Process Follows the shared default process — see ⏳ Hiring Process for details on each stage. 1 Recruiter — 30 min → 2 Hiring Manager — 30 min → 3 Case Study → 4 Final / Cultural Fit — 30 min → 5 References → 6 Offer ← Previous Senior Product Designer Next → Senior Affiliate Manager"},{"title":"Under the Hood — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"under-the-hood.html","text":"This article was written by our CTO & Co-founder, Michael Monin. ℹ️ Why this matters for candidates We're not a prototype. We run one of the most active AI companionship platforms in the world, on a lean, fast-moving Engineering team. If you care about scale, ownership, and shipping, read on. Scaling AI companionship — under the hood of a 10B request monolith 💎 Why We Use Rails Garry Tan recently noted that the world is \"sleeping\" on the combination of Ruby on Rails and AI-augmented coding. Because Rails is built on \"Convention Over Configuration,\" AI models like Claude can act autonomously within the codebase, resulting in massive productivity gains. At EverAI, we've turned that \"unlock\" into a reality at massive scale. We aren't just building an app; we are running a global infrastructure that handles: 28M Monthly Active Users 10B+ HTTP requests / 30 days 1 PB Monthly data traffic 📊 The raw numbers 10–12 billion HTTP requests in a typical 30-day window. Peaks push well north of 400M/day. 80M+ visits, 41M+ uniques, and we're serving a full petabyte of data (mostly images/videos — they're heavy). Last 30 days - Requests ⚒️ Keeping the queues happy Everything non-trivial is async: image, messages, notifications, ML inference queues, analytics events etc.. All flowing through Sidekiq. We process billions of jobs with basically zero backlog. On Rails. Sidekiq Jobs Throughput 💥 The database is... not small Single primary Postgres (plus read replicas) holding billions of messages, conversation, user profiles and more. Total size ~1.81TB and growing fast. Indexing and query optimization never sleep. Database We ship fast 🚀 Reviews typically land in under an hour. Engineers spend the vast majority of their time on new features, not firefighting. Heavy AI tool adoption in the codebase itself. PR velocity has been climbing steadily, with recent months routinely hitting 400–500+ merged PRs. Join Our Team We're still early in the journey to 500M+ users. The fun problems ahead: real-time WebSocket scaling for millions of concurrent chats, smarter caching of personalized conversation context, cost-efficient image/video generation at extreme volume, thoughtful monolith sharding, and making the whole system bulletproof under viral traffic spikes. The core stack is Ruby on Rails + Postgres + Redis + Sidekiq, but we're language-agnostic, strong modern backend/web experience matters way more than specific Rails years. If any of this sounds like the kind of scale you want to tackle every day, we're hiring senior backend engineers (full remote, Europe time zones preferred). ← Previous Engineering at EverAI Next → The EverAI Way"},{"title":"What We Do — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"what-we-do.html","text":"How It Started 🚀 It all started when our co-founders, Michael and Thomas, set out to create a WhatsApp chatbot assistant. But as they dove deeper into analyzing how users were interacting with it, they stumbled upon something surprising: people weren't just using it for assistance, they were using it romantically ! 💘 That \"aha\" moment sparked a bold new direction. Instead of sticking with the original plan, Michael and Thomas took a leap and decided to build something unique: Candy.ai, a platform that helps people foster deeper, more meaningful connections. Our Product & Technology We believe that AI isn't just about answering questions, it's about creating experiences that feel alive. We're focused on developing technology that allows users to step into stories, create characters, and explore their fantasies in a safe, fun, and judgment-free environment. Candy.ai Our journey began with Candy🍬 , the world's leading realistic AI companion platform. On the platform, we provide users with an array of tools to design and engage with AI companions in ways that reflect their personal vision. Here is what our technology allows users to do: Design & Customize: Users can design their own AI companions from the ground up, customizing appearance, personality traits, and voice, making each character truly unique. Chat through Text & AI Phone Calls: We take immersion to the next level. With just one tap, users can connect through a phone call and experience the full power of the AI they created, like talking to an old friend or meeting an exciting new one. Generate High-Fidelity Visuals: Users can describe a scene or idea, and our engine brings it to life. Whether they want a picture or a short video, a simple prompt generates a unique visual tailored to their imagination. Pushing the Boundaries of Immersion 🚀 We don't just settle for \"standard\" features. We are constantly shipping industry-first innovations to make the experience deeper and more engaging: Advanced Image & Video Tech: We've enabled users to turn static images (including Anime styles) into motion with 5-second and 10-second animations. Group Chat: Users can now step into multi-character dynamics, where companions interact not just with the user, but with each other! 🤯 Hyper-Realistic \"Live Action\": We have introduced Live Action models that blur the line between AI and reality, offering a level of visual detail that feels completely authentic. The Explore Feed: We created an engaging Feed where users can discover high-quality content and characters created by our world-class content teams, providing endless inspiration and entertainment. Memory System: It's not just a chat bot; it remembers. Users can now build long-term context with their companions, who recall specific details and shared moments to build a genuine bond. Creative Mode (New! 🎨): We recently launched Creative Mode, giving users a \"sandbox\" to generate images and videos freely from prompts without being tied to a specific character. It's pure generative freedom. How It's Going 🔥 Since our launch in September 2023 , Candy AI has absolutely taken off, becoming the largest platform of its kind worldwide in record time! With 20 million unique users per month , we've earned our place among the top 4 Generative AI web products globally, standing shoulder-to-shoulder with the biggest names in the industry. In under a year, we've hit eight-figure annualized revenue , a milestone that speaks to the incredible growth of our platform. Now, over 18 months in, we have scaled significantly past that milestone. And we're not the only ones who've noticed: investors have too! We've successfully raised $10 million in funding , cementing Candy.ai as one of the fastest-growing companies in the space. Our community of 50 Million users is a testament to the platform's incredible appeal and impact, particularly in two of the fastest-growing Gen AI categories: content generation and companion . To read the full article, visit this page . According to Harvard Business Review, Generative AI in 2025 has shifted from technical use cases to emotional, personal, and human-centric applications . To read the full article, visit this page . 🧠 Bottom Line CandyAI isn't just riding the wave, it's shaping it. In a world where users are actively turning to GenAI for companionship, intimacy, and purpose, CandyAI is building exactly what people are asking for , and doing it earlier and better than most. We couldn't be prouder of how far we've come, and can't wait to see what the future holds for us! And the best part? We're just getting started! Our Future (And Your Role in It) We're not stopping here; and we need your help writing the next chapter. Coming soon, we're working on: AI Chat in Local Languages : We are actively expanding our language capabilities to 16+ languages to make global interaction easier. Improved AI-generated videos : Users' stories will come to life in moving pictures, turning words into vivid animations. Currently we offer 10 second videos, with ample improvement opportunities. AI Live Streaming: We've set ourselves an ambitious goal: to be the first in the world to launch AI Live Streaming for our industry. We believe adoption will be off the charts , with use cases spanning far and wide. AR/VR integration : Soon, users will step into their stories , living their fantasies through immersive AR/VR experiences. 👑 We acquired 50M users in 2 years, our goal is to reach 100M users in the next 12 months, and 500M after. To achieve that, we're looking for exceptional talent ready to ship & scale world-first AI products fast, and co-create with us this category defining business. The next few years will be transformative, and we're inviting you to be part of that journey. ← Previous Who We Are Next → Safety and Ethics"},{"title":"Who We Are — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"who-we-are.html","text":"Our Vision EverAI - Building the future of AI Companionship. At EverAI , we're shaping what it means to connect with AI. With 50 Million users and counting , we're not just building products, we're creating entirely new categories. Our vision is clear: \"To combat loneliness and boredom through immersive and lifelike AI experiences.\" We are the team behind: Candy.ai : The world's largest AI companionship platform , redefining companionship for millions. All of this is governed by our proprietary moderation system, EverGuard : an internal AI designed to ensure everything we build is safe, ethical, and human-first . 🪄 As part of the team, you'll help bring these stories to life, building the future of AI companionship, where imagination knows no limits. Our Values Meet the Team Our team is made up of a fully remote group of A-players from Tier 1 tech. We move fast, and care deeply about what we build, and who we build it with. Leading our journey is a founding team with deep entrepreneurial roots and a proven track record of success. Having built and scaled multiple web products from the ground up, all the way to IPO , they bring the kind of expertise and leadership that transforms ambitious ideas into reality. Thomas Lacroix Co-founder & CMO Michael Monin Co-founder & CTO Alexis Soulopoulos CEO Dr. Maruša Fasano CFO/Legal • 8+ years in Customer Acquisition & E-commerce Growth • Serial-entrepreneur: Curatible (sold to Blackstone) and MTK Digital (exited / 0→$20m revenue) • 9+ years as CTO / COO, 1+ year in AI, LLM • Serial-entrepreneur: MTK Digital (exited / 0→$20m revenue) and Zipchat (exited / AI Chatbot for E-commerce brands) • 10+ years in Tech Executive Leadership • Co-Founder Mad Paws Holdings (from 0 to IPO) • Forbes 30U30 + Deloitte TechFast50 '22 & '23 • 25+ years in Finance, Strategy, M&A • Ex-CFO/M&A @Curatible (exited to Blackstone) • Ex-President of the Board @SotremoSA (exited) • Co-founder/CFO @SoftOne (exited) At EverAI , we are lucky to have an incredible group of people who bring their expertise from world-renowned companies, such as: We're a mix of smart, passionate people who love solving problems and pushing the boundaries of AI. When you join us, you'll work alongside colleagues who are not just experts in what they do, but are also excited to share, learn, and have fun building something incredible together. What Sets Us Apart Besides our Team described in the above section, EverAI is a unique opportunity because: 📈 Exponential Growth : From 50M users in 2 years, to 100M next, and 500M beyond. 🚀 Track Record of Category-Creating Innovation : We consistently launch world-first AI applications. We are setting the pace, not following it. 🌍 Global Impact : Top-tier user growth, real-world adoption, and cultural relevance. 🛡️ Ethical Core : Finally, we built the world's most advanced AI Content Moderation, it's for users, technology & financial partners, and for attracting the right talent. Our dedicated Compliance team, led by our Ethics & Compliance Officer and working closely with our AI teams, ensures that ethics and compliance are embedded in everything we build and do: 🛡️ EverGuard, our proprietary AI-Powered Moderation Technology Our advanced AI technology protects against any prohibited content, ensuring a safe environment for all users. ✅ Audited and Transparent We're independently audited by a trusted audit firm and overseen by our Board of Directors, guaranteeing accountability. Payment providers, banks, and other partners regularly audit us to meet strict compliance standards. 🏦 Investor-Backed Stability We've raised a $10M seed round from prominent investors who conducted rigorous due diligence before investing. By joining EverAI, you'll be part of a team that values integrity, innovation, and trust at every level. The team at our annual company gathering - CandyCon26 in Buenos Aires! ← Previous Candidate Handbook Next → What We Do"},{"title":"Why Join Us? — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"why-join-us.html","text":"Why Work at EverAI 🔥 Ambitious AI Project We're only scratching the surface of what AI can do. With ambitious new features like Live Streaming on the horizon, your contributions will have a direct and visible impact on shaping the future of our product. ⭐ A 5-Star International Team Elite 100% Remote Team from Tier 1 tech companies , with a culture of ownership, velocity, and radical creativity. Our founding team has a proven track record, taking startups from zero to millions of users, all the way to IPO. Work alongside seasoned entrepreneurs , learn from the best, and build a product that reaches hundreds of millions. 🚀 Huge Traction Since our product launch in September 2023, we've grown to 50 Million Users . You'll be joining a company that's already proving its potential and scaling rapidly. 💬 Annual Performance Reviews We see this as a collaborative process, where feedback flows both ways. Through collaborative annual performance reviews , regular check-ins, and open communication and feedback, we ensure your goals align with our mission. Your growth is immensely important to us. 🪴 Career Progression and Growth Opportunities As we scale rapidly, so will your growth. Whether it's mastering new tools, exploring emerging technologies, or tackling ambitious projects, we'll give you the resources and freedom to grow your expertise and take your career to the next level. Our Benefits and Perks 💥 Choose Your Path Whether you're looking for a regular contract or prefer being a contractor , we've got you covered. As long as you're committed to the journey, we're excited to have you on board! 📍 Work From Anywhere Full remote , no strings attached. Whether it's your home office or a beachside bungalow, you can choose where you do your best work . We trust you to create the environment that fuels you. 🌴 4 Weeks of Paid Time Off We know the best ideas come when you're well-rested and recharged. Enjoy 20 days of PTO annually to reset, explore, or simply unwind. 👩‍👩‍👦‍👦 Annual Team Gatherings While we thrive as a remote-first team, we know nothing beats face-to-face connections. That's why we organize yearly meet-ups to bring everyone together , brainstorm, and strengthen the bonds that make us a powerful team. ❤️‍🩹 Health & Wellness Support All contractors receive a $100 monthly allowance to support health insurance costs + Access to unlimited 1:1 sessions with psychologists and lifestyle experts through OpenUp (also available to up to three of your family members). 📚 Learning Budget Fuel your growth with a learning budget , which you can use for courses, books, conferences, or any resource that helps you sharpen your skills and stay ahead. 🏢 Co-Working Space Budget To make remote work more engaging and social, every team member can work from a co-working space up to twice per month , with a budget of €35 / $40 per visit . It's a simple way to connect with others, stay inspired, and enjoy a change of scenery whenever you need it. 💻 Company Laptop & Equipment You'll be equipped for success with a company laptop , plus a monitor budget of up to $250 and a keyboard/mouse/mic/headphones budget of up to $150 . ⚡ Top-Tier AI Tools for the Best Talent You'll get access to tools like ChatGPT, Gemini, Cursor, Hugging Face, and others , to experiment, push boundaries, and bring your boldest ideas to life. Some of our values displayed at CandyCon 2025. EverAI values: Aim Bigger, Go Faster Enjoy The Journey Make It Happen Stay Hungry, Stay Curious Own It, All of It Conquer Together through Teamwork Reality Check: Is EverAI Right For You? We value transparency above all else. EverAI is an incredible place to grow, but it is not for everyone . We are a high-performance team moving at breakneck speed. We want all our team members to be happy and motivated at work, so to save your time and ours, please read the following. You might not enjoy working here if: 🚧 You prefer heavy structure and fixed processes We build the plane while flying it. Processes change, priorities shift, and we often have to figure things out on the fly. If you need a strict playbook or a manager to tell you exactly what to do every day, this probably won't be a good place for you. 🐌 You have a low tolerance for fast iteration We ship features fast (sometimes in hours, not weeks). We test constantly. If you need 100% certainty or prefer to spend weeks perfecting a plan before executing, our pace will feel uncomfortable. 🙅 You expect a rigid role without ownership We value \"Own It, All of It\". We operate with clear ownership. If something is broken, we fix it. We trust A-players to step outside their lane to fix problems and make decisions without waiting for approval. If you prefer strict job descriptions or rely on getting everyone to agree before moving forward, this isn't the environment for you. 🫣 You dislike being accountable and humble With great freedom comes great responsibility. We trust you to work from anywhere, but we expect you to own your outcomes. If things go wrong, we expect you to raise your hand, learn, and fix it, not hide it. 🧪 You are uncomfortable with experimentation, ambiguity, or frequent change We take risks. We try different things constantly to see what happens. Some things work; some don't. You need to be resilient enough to fail, learn, and try again immediately. ← Previous The EverAI Way Next → Our Recruitment Process"},{"title":"Growth — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"growth.html","text":"🚀 Growth roles drive acquisition, retention, and partner-led revenue for EverAI / Candy.ai. Click a role family below for its full brief, screening criteria, and sourcing guidance. 📈 Performance Marketing Four distinct roles across two acquisition tracks and two seniority levels. Each track has its own hiring bar and sourcing guidance — always use the specific track brief. Performance Marketer — All Tracks ↗ Junior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB ↗ Senior Performance Marketer — Adult RTB ↗ Junior Performance Marketer — Mainstream ↗ Senior Performance Marketer — Mainstream ↗ 🤝 Affiliate & Lifecycle Senior Affiliate Manager ↗ Senior Lifecycle Marketing Manager ↗"},{"title":"R&D — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"rd.html","text":"🧪 R&D builds and ships EverAI / Candy.ai's product. Click a role below for its full brief, screening criteria, and sourcing guidance. 👩‍💻 Senior Ruby on Rails Engineer ↗ 🎥 AI Cinematic Video Editor ↗ 🎨 Senior Product Designer ↗ 🔒 Security Engineer ↗ 🧭 Senior Product Manager ↗"},{"title":"Operations — EverAI Partner Hiring Wiki","url":"operations.html","text":"🛠️ Operations keeps EverAI / Candy.ai running safely and efficiently. Click a role below for its full brief, screening criteria, and sourcing guidance. 🛡️ Content Moderator ↗ 📊 Business Analyst ↗"}];
